52021013733915070132694421338250\"","\"751.50\"","\"2325.3162498\"","\"116.26581249\"","\"193.77635415\"","\"1453.322656125\"","\"axis\"","\"value\"","\"result\"","\"bull_esop_claims\"","\"intraperiod_cycles\"","\"margin_x_terminal_k\"","\"growth_x_unbilled\"","\"roundtrip_execution_cost_each_side\"","\"case\"","\"GOV3\"","\"4.76\"","\"0.84\"","\"0.56\"","\"6.20\"","\"2.80\"","\"1.05\"","\"5.70\"","\"2.45\"","\"1.40\"","\"0.70\"","\"PASS\"","\"Avoid — governance\"","\"GOV4\"","\"4.96\"","\"6.1900\"","\"1.2400\"","\"6.2\"","\"G1_FAIL\"","\"5.56\"","\"FAIL\"","\"G3_FAIL\"","\"5.6\"","\"6.3400\"","\"1.3900\"","\"Distressed / funding failure\"","\"G2_HOLD\"","\"6.3\"","\"NS_GOV3\"","\"2.52\"","\"0.68\"","\"2.84\"","\"5.72\"","\"2.8\"","\"1.7600\"","\"7.65\"","\"1.8\"","\"CASH4_NO_CAP\"","\"5.66\"","\"5.7\"","\"6.30\"","\"6.3650\"","\"1.4150\"","\"6.4\"","\"PERSISTENT_CAP3\"","\"5.38\"","\"0.36\"","\"5.4\"","\"5.90\"","\"0.45\"","\"6.2950\"","\"1.3450\"","\"TRANSIENT_CAP3\"","\"5.9\"","\"MOAT-1\"","\"1.72\"","\"2.24\"","\"6.92\"","\"2.2\"","\"6.9\"","\"1.6100\"","\"8.6300\"","\"1.6\"","\"8.6\"","\"MOAT+1\"","\"2.12\"","\"2.64\"","\"7.32\"","\"2.6\"","\"7.3\"","\"1.7100\"","\"8.7300\"","\"DUR-1\"","\"1.82\"","\"2.34\"","\"7.02\"","\"2.3\"","\"7.0\"","\"1.10\"","\"1.80\"","\"8.10\"","\"1.6350\"","\"8.6550\"","\"DUR+1\"","\"2.02\"","\"2.54\"","\"7.22\"","\"2.5\"","\"7.2\"","\"1.50\"","\"1.20\"","\"2.20\"","\"8.50\"","\"1.6850\"","\"8.7050\"","\"Research; critical financial-reliability hold; not a trading instruction\"","\"# ROX Hi-Tech Limited | SME research | v3.0\\n\\n## 1. Executive Verdict\\n\\n**Hold — unresolved financial reliability. BQS NS; GQS NS; IAS NS.** ROX sells and integrates enterprise IT hardware, software and support, with an emerging managed-services proposition. Its two-decade operating history, OEM relationships and newly operational delivery facilities provide a credible business opportunity, but do not establish proprietary software economics. FY26 invoiced revenue shifted toward products while services contracted. More importantly, reported operating cash includes borrowing movements, the consolidated comparative cash-flow construction is not comparable, unbilled revenue and profit/share reconciliations remain unresolved, and most reported cash is in deposits linked to credit facilities. These are specific verification problems despite unmodified audit opinions, not a fraud finding. At ₹75.15 on 19 October 2026, a roughly 194.78crore issued-share valuation cannot be called attractive from the headline 11.99× P/E. This is a funding-sensitive integration/managed-services transition to investigate, not an evidence-backed compounder. Reconciled accounts, collected contract assets and independently verified available liquidity, rather than a lower quote alone, would change the conclusion. [S01, printed148–175, Notes17–20/30/32; S09; E02–E15.]\\n\\n## 2. Research Header, Gates and Data Confidence\\n\\n- Exact issuer: ROX Hi-Tech Limited, formerly ROX Trading and Systems Private Limited. NSE ROXHITECH; ISIN INE0PDJ01013; CIN L51506TN2002PLC048598. Indian Accounting Standards under Indian GAAP/AS, not assumed Ind AS. Incorporation March2002 is not confused with November2023 listing. [S01, Notes1–2; S03, cover/general information; S09 security row.]\\n- Information cutoff:20 October2026. Market observation:19 October2026 close₹75.15, last₹75.00; not a live executable offer. All monetary financial tables below are ₹crore unless expressly labelled otherwise.\\n- Current issued claims:25,918,614 after13 October allotment. The dated security master still shows23,968,614, a lag explicitly overridden by the primary allotment. Warrants-only potential claims30,480,470 include2,061,856 older and2,500,000 new warrants, before separate ESOP uncertainty. The conservative remaining-plan overlay461,862 gives30,942,332 total economic claims, not actual issued shares. Weighted historical EPS denominators are different. [S06, pp.1–2; S21, p.1; S22, warrant terms/dilution table.]\\n- Latest annual financials:FY26; parent historical series FY21–26 and separately FY25–26 group. No invented quarterly/H1FY27 cash flow and no overlapping TTM. Horizonfive years, nominal INR equity hurdle15%, sensitivities12/18%; ₹5 lakh illustrative position, not a supplied user holding.\\n- Confidence: High on identity, source wording, observed daily turnover and allotments; Medium on business positioning and execution statements; Low on normalized owner earnings, underlying organic growth, comparable cash and incremental returns. An audited label does not eliminate contradictory audited schedules.\\n\\n| Gate | Finding | Consequence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| G1 governance | Hold — unresolved stewardship/reporting and RPT reconciliation; no substantiated diversion or severe minority harm | GOV NS, no unsupported governance-fraud override |\\n| G2 financial reliability | Hold — unresolved material cash-flow, contract-asset, consolidated-scope and profit/EPS issues | IAS NS and no favourable new-entry classification |\\n| G3 funding/survival | Conditional: no reported default, but near-full limits and large working-capital assets | Conditional stress only; an assumed model breach is not proof of actual default |\\n| G4 tradability | Conditional: 1600 share lot, observed ST series, limited participation and incomplete restriction/depth evidence | Not suspended or automatically untradeable; practical exit limits remain |\\n\\n## 3. Scorecard and Calculation Audit\\n\\n|Factor|Score|Confidence|Evidence and reason|\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n|GOV|NS|Low|E05, E11, E14, E15, E23: Stewardship not scoreable until repeated reporting, RPT and capital reconciliation issues resolve.|\\n|MOAT|4|Medium|E02, E17, E20: Relationships, OEM certifications and integrated delivery are useful but contestable; gross hardware economics dominate disclosed invoicing.|\\n|REV|NS|Low|E02, E03, E16, E22: Gross reported3/5year growth can be calculated but material unbilled/perimeter and product/service changes obstruct reliable underlying expansion.|\\n|DUR|5|Medium|E02, E16, E17: Cloud, security, enterprise modernisation and installed-client cross-sell form accessible avenues; public orderbook lacks cash/margin reconciliation.|\\n|CAP|NS|Low|E07, E08, E09, E13: Incremental capital proxy exposed but unresolved cash, consolidation and profit bridges make reliable score unavailable.|\\n|CASH|3|Medium|E03, E04, E06, E08, E22: Persistent debt-funded working capital, aged balances and weak borrowing-adjusted cash are material recurring weaknesses.|\\n|BAL|NS|Low|E11, E12, E13, E15: Large restricted deposits, near-full lines, uncertain current cash and recent financing prevent reliable survival score.|\\n|EXEC|4|Medium|E16, E03, E13: FY26 missed stated20%growth aspiration; promised WC reduction not achieved on combined metrics.|\\n|EARN|NS|Low|E09, E10, E15: Conflicting profit/EPS and changing dilution obstruct dependable per-share recurring earnings scoring.|\\n|R|NS|Low|E09, E18: Conditional paths do not underwrite a probability-weighted expected return.|\\n|D|NS|Low|E12, E13, E18: Survival depends on actual drawablecash,collectionsandrefinancingstillunverified.|\\n|P|NS|Low|E09, E15, E18: Reverse thresholds computed but unreliablebasecannotestablishattractiveness.|\\n|L|4|Medium|E19, E24: Starting5from5–10days;explicitonepointdeductionfor1600-sharelotandST/circuitconstraints.|\\n\\n|Composite|Known contribution|Coverage|Exact raw bounds|Cap|Final|Post-cap display bounds|\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n|BQS|1.92|48.00%|2.44–7.12|None|NS|2.4–7.1|\\n|GQS|1.30|30.00%|2.00–8.30|5|NS|2.0–5.0|\\n|IAS|0.40|10.00%|1.6600–8.6800|None|NS|1.7–8.7|\\n\\nWeights are unchanged from the recovered v3.0 master. BQS: GOV20%, MOAT20%, REV12%, DUR10%, CAP12%, CASH10%, BAL8%, EXEC8%. Known contributions are0.80+0.50+0.30+0.32=1.92, covering48%. GQS: REV40%, DUR20%, EARN15%, CAP15%, CASH10%; known1.00+0.30=1.30, covering30%. IAS: exact final BQS25%, R35%, D20%, P10%, L10%; onlyL contributes0.40, covering10%. Nested BQS bounds are propagated, never substituted as a midpoint or as a score.\\n\\nPersistent poor cash realization supports CASH3 and the stated GQS cap5. The aggregate remains **NS**, not5. No governance or funding cap is silently applied merely because evidence is missing. Missing-factor bounds are mathematical possibilities, not statistical intervals or a ranking. Exact unrounded Decimal arithmetic and all contributions are in scores.json. Moving MOAT4 by±1 changes BQS bounds by±0.20 and IAS bounds by±0.05; moving DUR5 by±1 changes BQS bounds by±0.10, GQS by±0.20 and IAS by±0.025. These uncertain known judgments do not cure the missing critical factors. Boundary tests separately exercise GOV3/4, G1/G3 failure, G2 hold, NS with caps and persistent versus transient capital problems.\\n\\nL starts at5 for approximately5–10 theoretical participation days; one disclosed point is deducted for large lot/ST/circuit/depth constraints. No extra liquidity penalty is subsequently added to IAS.\\n\\n## 4. Business Overview\\n\\nROX sources enterprise IT products and software, designs and installs infrastructure, and provides support, facilities management, cybersecurity, cloud, digital transformation and application services. OEM/channel relationships include IBM, Cisco and SAP. These relationships help sell complex projects but the OEM normally owns the underlying technology. Customer logos and partner awards are not proof of exclusive supply rights, intellectual property, subscription retention or pricing power. No independently reconciled ARR, software retention/cohorts, licensed-IP gross margin or SaaS unit economics is available. [S03, business section pp.102–134; S11, business/partner slides; E01–E02.]\\n\\nFY26 consolidated operating revenue₹202.9826 comprises invoiced products/services₹172.5090 plus a P&L unbilled-revenue contribution₹30.4736. Invoices comprise domestic products₹151.8876, SEZ products₹4.3016, services₹16.0432 and FMS₹0.2766. Product invoicing is90.54% of invoices, not a disclosed90.54% of final total recognized revenue because the unbilled component has no comparable product/service split. FY25 services/FMS were₹36.0863 and products₹123.8447. Therefore a blanket IT-services valuation ignores the actual disclosed mix. Product resale can create large gross sales with modest retained value, while integration projects tie cash in inventory, acceptance milestones and unbilled work. Recurring support can be better economics, but its revenue and capital returns have not been separately demonstrated. [S01, printed164, Note20; E02–E03.]\\n\\nThe business has Indian enterprise customers plus overseas subsidiaries. Consolidation begins only FY25; a two-year group comparison is not a five-year organic history. Overseas audit reliance is discussed below. Commissioning a50-seat facility is potential delivery capacity, not proof of utilization, paid seats or revenue per employee. [S01, subsidiary and audit other-matter disclosures, printed141–147; S02, PDF151/155; S05, operating update.]\\n\\n## 5. Moat / Industry Position\\n\\n| Proposed mechanism | Supporting evidence | Durability test and failure mode |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Installed-customer knowledge and integrated delivery | Long operating record, OEM certifications, broad project capability | Renewal/retention and service contribution ND; capable integrators can compete; OEMs retain technology bargaining power |\\n| Technical qualification and execution | SAP/IBM/Cisco positioning; management reports NOC/SOC live and clients onboard | Certifications are renewable and not exclusive; people can leave, new systems displace old expertise |\\n| Scale/cross-sell | Existing enterprise relationships and management-reported new transformation clients | Must produce cash-paid higher-value services rather than more low-retained-value hardware |\\n| Customer switching costs | Integration effort can make disruption costly | Purchase-order contracting and multiple supplier options weaken contractual lock-in; no quantified switching-cost evidence |\\n\\nProspectus FY23 top10 customers were46.68% of sales and top5 approximately41.45%; the FY26 presentation shows historical FY25 top10 at35%. That is useful reported diversification, but current FY26 top10 and vendor concentration percentages are ND. Contracts are generally purchase-order based, without broad long-term customer volume guarantees; the prospectus discloses no fixed vendor pricing or automatic pass-through protection. More customers do not establish low dependence on particular OEMs or a small number of large projects.\\n\\n**Named economic peers, primary-source comparison.** Dynacons Systems & Solutions, Orient Technologies and Allied Digital are relevant integration/managed-services comparisons, not interchangeable valuation twins. Dynacons FY26 consolidated revenue₹1424.2834, total PAT₹84.8124, owner PAT₹84.7352 and CFO₹46.1345 versus₹66.0423 prior demonstrate greater scale but uneven cash. Its₹155.3178 lease liabilities and₹29.9084 lease cash payments complicate an asset-light EBITDA comparison. Its presentation shows data-centre34%, networking12%, workplace31% and managed-services23% mix. Orient FY26 revenue₹869.5445, reported EBITDA includingOI₹49.1473 and owner PAT₹4.5700 reflect₹23.6833 exceptional expenses: discontinued-customer costs roughly₹19.60 and labour-code liability₹4.08. CFO is−₹19.4101 and capex₹63.0047. The ₹19.5989customer-discontinuation write-off is an economic execution/capitalization loss even when labelled exceptional. Its solutions₹418.3724 versus services₹451.1721 mix and revised segment reporting are more informative than a single P/E. Allied FY26 presentation reports roughly₹968 revenue and adjusted EBITDA₹112 includingOI, explicitly excluding₹36 provision; CFO−₹78.52 versus₹92.27 is a warning, not evidence of clean sector cash generation. Its older CRISIL rationale describes lengthy working capital and an ECL provision. Peer strengths and weaknesses support skepticism of gross-sales multiples and unadjusted EBITDA, not a mechanically assigned premium or a claim that all peers are superior. No current peer trading multiple is invented. [S12, PDF154–157; S13, slides9/23/35–36; S15, printed45/185–186, Note33; S14, slides34–36; S18, working-capital/rating rationale; E20/E21/E25.]\\n\\n## 6. Revenue Growth & Scale\\n\\n|Window|Endpoints revenue|Reported CAGR|ΔNOPAT|Δbroad IC|Diagnostic ΔNOPAT/ΔIC|Capital/investment residual|\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n|2023–2026|133.33 → 207.92|15.97%|2.48|128.71|1.93%|-0.04|\\n|2021–2026|64.07 → 207.92|26.55%|18.88|165.08|11.43%|-0.15|\\n\\nSources/calculation: [S01/S02/S03; historical_metrics.json, windows.] Ten-year revenue CAGR is unavailable because a comparableFY16endpoint was not retrieved; no backfilled estimate is supplied.\\n\\nThe reported parent sequence₹64.0718,102.8622,133.3279,176.0586,186.5068,207.9243 shows real commercial scaling worth investigating, including annual rupee additions₹38.7904,30.4657,42.7307,10.4482 and21.4175. It is not penalized merely for starting small. FY21, however, is a pandemic-affected low base, and later unbilled recognition and group formation distort a simple organic-CAGR interpretation. Group FY26 revenue grew8.28%, versus parent11.48%; parent and group must not be spliced. [S03, restated financials pp.43–45/F1 onward; S02, FY24 comparatives; S01, parent and group P&L; historical_inputs.json.]\\n\\nThe FY25–26 invoiced bridge is products+₹32.3445, services/FMS−₹19.7665, giving invoice growth₹12.5780 or7.86%. The additional unbilled P&L contribution increased₹2.9472. Recognized group sales rose₹15.5252. This bridge identifies product/service mix, not units, prices or customer-level organic volume. FX, acquisitions, like-for-like customer gains/losses and price/volume are not separately reconciled. In particular, unbilled balance grew₹39.8237, but P&L says₹30.4736: the₹9.3501 bridge is unresolved and matches a prior subsidiary-sales number. That numerical coincidence is a reconciliation question, not proof of fabrication. REV remains NS until genuine underlying expansion can be measured reliably. [S01, printed163–164, Notes19–20; E02–E03; calculated bridge in historical_metrics.json.]\\n\\n## 7. Growth Quality & Reinvestment Runway\\n\\nDemand for modernization, cloud, data centres, cyber controls and enterprise applications offers accessible work through existing customer relationships. The useful bottom-up question is the number of funded, accepted and collected projects plus paid service contracts, not a global IT-spending TAM. Management reports seven new digital-transformation clients, a live NOC/SOC and a50-seat Trichy SEZ centre; contracted recurring revenue, utilization, unit pricing and customer profitability remain ND. No unsupported claim of capacity-limited exponential SaaS growth is made. [S05, June15 call pp.2–13; S11, delivery-capacity slides; E16.]\\n\\nThe model therefore uses explicit revenue, operating-margin and cash-day assumptions rather than fabricated customer counts. Base revenue grows10% annually from an8% above FY26 bridge run rate; bull18%; bear−5%. These are analyst scenarios, not guidance. Every incremental rupee requires inventory, receivables/contract assets, supplier credit, opex, cash taxes, maintenance and growth capex. A separate₹4.4571 security/margin-deposit bucket scales with the revenue run rate, with additional deposits paid in cash and no assumed release on contraction. The0/1/2×deposit-intensity sensitivities test that requirement. Maintenance is estimated at1.5% of revenue, stressed1–2%; incremental fixed investment5% of revenue additions is an assumption, not a disclosed project budget. A revenue/fixed-asset capacity ceiling10× prevents unlimited revenue with no assets, but is not evidence of actual capacity. Failure to obtain paid-seat/project economics keeps CAP/DUR confidence constrained. [Analyst assumptions: model_inputs.json/model_engine.py; S01, Note14 deposits.]\\n\\nParent broad invested-capital proxies and3/5 year changes are exposed above; they include CWIP and operating balances, not merely cash capex. They are accounting diagnostics with unresolved classification/perimeter bridges, not project IRRs. FY26 consolidated operating IC, separately reconstructed from detailed notes, is about₹177.71 versus₹134.50 prior; its NOPAT fell, so current additional capital has not yet demonstrated attractive returns. A13–17% nominal INR cost-of-capital range is a judgment for leveraged, illiquid integration economics, not a universal WACC. Terminal scenarios use14–18% with wider13/20% tests and explicitly fund sustainable growth at an assumed15% incremental return. Commissioned facilities may require a lag, but the report does not assume their eventual profit rescues poor observed returns. GQS remains NS with a5cap on its bound due to persistent cash weakness. [S01, printed148–165, Notes5–19; S02/S03 historical statements; historical_metrics.json, capital bridges; E07–E13.]\\n\\n## 8. Management, Governance & Execution\\n\\nJim Rakesh and Sukanya Rakesh are the principal promoter/managing leadership. A long operating history and promoter ownership can align incentives but do not replace minority-owner cash outcomes. FY26 RPT service sales are₹4.3637 versus₹1.0249, related receivables₹7.1768 versus₹2.2467 and payables₹1.3238 versus₹3.6708. KMP remuneration₹1.3125 plus sitting fees₹0.1460 is disclosed; the standalone related-party service note₹5.4039 conflicts with its revenue note₹4.3637. Commercial related-party activity is not automatically abusive, but collectability, pricing and scope need reconciliation. Current promoter encumbrance and post-allotment free float are not fully verified, so neither a zero-pledge assertion nor a precise current promoter percentage is manufactured. [S03, promoter background; S01, printed167–168, Note30 and standalone Note20/30; E14.]\\n\\n| Dated statement/action | Observable outcome by cutoff | Assessment |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| May29,2025 call: around20% growth expectation and working-capital reduction | FY26 parent11.48%, group8.28%; billed AR fell, but billed+unbilled and inventory rose | Growth expectation missed; narrow debtor decline is not total cash improvement |\\n| June15,2026 call: NOC/SOC operational, clients onboard, seven transformation additions | Management reports commercialization and50-seat office; audited FY26 mix still hardware-heavy | Positive commissioning evidence; recurring economics not yet verified |\\n| IPO capital for delivery infrastructure and working capital | FY25 CWIP₹18.096 moves into FY26 computer/software assets; large operating asset expansion | Transfer is not equivalent to new FY26 cash capex or proof of returns |\\n| July25 EGM preferential proposal | Oct13 shares/warrants allotted; intended₹9.01 new business,₹4.50WC,₹4.50general purposes bySep2028 | Future warrant subscription is optional; objects are not actual use-of-proceeds evidence |\\n| May29 and July15 corrections after exchange queries | Revised results and later AR still retain identified CF ambiguities | Responding is positive; material bridges remain unresolved |\\n\\nThe18-page FY23 issuer file contains AGM/directors material but no actual audit/annexures. It reports Sundaresan & Subramanian resignation24April2023, L U Krishnan appointment and resignation29June citing preoccupation, then same-day P P N appointment. This management-disclosed chronology is not evidence of adverse outgoing findings. Its FY23/FY22 PAT₹15.3971/₹1.5409 differs from prospectus-restated₹15.3297/₹1.5131; revenue matches, and profit vintages remain separate. [S28, PDF7/12–14; S03, restated statements; E31.]\\n\\nFY24 original annual-results audit byPPN & Company is unmodified. After two damaged downloads, a readable official AGM/full annual-report copy was recovered. Its complete audit, CARO and IFC were inspected: unmodified opinion, affirmative IFC, positive audit trail, bank returns agreeing with books and no reported default, fraud or resignation. FY24 Note27 records a historical₹3.5939crore Ingram Micro cheque-bounce proceeding, with principal discharged but petition disposal awaited. Later contingent-claim notes are nil; court closure was not independently established. This is not current unpaid principal or a fraud finding. The pending charge on a₹11.60lakh vehicle loan is minor compliance context. [S26, PDF41–45 and printed100/104–105, Notes10/27; S01/S02, Note25.] FY25 and FY26 complete parent/group audit reports, KAMs, CARO, IFC and financial notes were inspected. FY25 CARO says an auditor resigned during the year without outgoing concerns; do not treat that statement as misconduct. FY26 Krishaan &Co opinions/IFC are unmodified/affirmative. KAMs focus on inventory, receivables and payables; only some confirmations are received and book balances are adopted for others. Subsidiaries are management-certified: FY25 audit literally describes assets₹10.9839/revenue₹10.3006, FY26 ₹0.2356/₹0.0880, an unresolved scope/unit contraction despite continuing entities. Group IFC conclusions likewise rely on management certificates. [S19, complete results audit; S26, full audit/CARO/IFC and historical litigation; S02, PDF107–117/151–155; S01, printed102–111/140–147; E05/E22/E27.]\\n\\nFY26 parent CARO records₹3.1594 FY25 self-assessment tax outstanding more than six months; group CARO says no adverse remarks, requiring reconciliation. No loan default or fraud is reported. The1 October independent-director resignation states no other material reasons and is not treated as proof of an audit dispute. JulyEGM beneficial-owner details were subsequently corrected from not applicable to named individuals, and investor nameRay Invest toRaynvvest. Disclosure corrections merit verification, not an unsupported allegation of hidden ownership.\\n\\n## 9. Financial Forensics\\n\\n|FY standalone|Revenue|EBITDA ex OI|EBIT ex OI|PAT|CFO as filed|Cash capex|Reported FCF|Debt|Reported cash|Broad IC proxy|\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n|2021|64.07|1.07|0.92|0.66|3.15|1.11|2.04|11.35|3.37|15.69|\\n|2022|102.86|4.15|3.93|1.51|-4.87|0.20|-5.07|17.95|1.49|25.99|\\n|2023|133.33|23.02|22.78|15.33|3.73|0.69|3.04|22.58|0.01|52.06|\\n|2024|176.06|31.79|31.10|21.24|-33.72|7.97|-41.69|21.29|25.17|97.02|\\n|2025|186.51|28.52|27.47|19.32|23.61|22.89|0.72|46.58|27.45|135.98|\\n|2026|207.92|27.80|26.09|17.64|3.19|1.31|1.88|68.88|27.24|180.77|\\n\\nSources: [S03, prospectus restatementFY21–23; S02, FY24comparatives; S01, FY25–26parent; S19, originalFY24vintage separately. Exact figures/source IDs in historical_inputs.json.]\\n\\n**Cash is not simply PAT less capex.** FY26 consolidated revenue₹202.9826 less product cost₹150.0922, employee₹15.9058 and other operating expense₹10.5776 gives recurring EBITDA₹26.4070 and EBIT₹24.7016 afterDA₹1.7054. Printed EBITDA₹29.1156 includesOI₹2.7086. Finance expense₹6.5464 and taxes then affect owner earnings. P&L PAT₹16.2435, EPS/reserve-linked₹16.9275 and directors' summary₹16.19 are not a single verified normalized owner numerator. The₹0.6840 exceptional line and EPS differences7.11/7.37 versus7.41/7.38 remain open. A simple EBIT less finance, taxed25%, is only a diagnostic, not an audit reconciliation. Stock-option compensation expense and its cash-flow addback are not separately reconciled, so no SBC addback is made to normalized profit or owner cash. The conservative claim overlay captures dilution, not a claim that employee compensation is free. [S27, PDF13 accounting policy; S01, printed82 and expense notes.] Rent₹1.8496 is already in opex; do not add a second rental deduction or manufacture IndAS lease debt. The asset schedule includes a leasing-asset line but does not establish an omitted quantified lease liability. [S01, printed149/157/164–168, P&L and Notes20–24/32; E09–E10.]\\n\\nFY26 as-filed group CFO₹3.4114 includes₹25.4567 labelled short-term provisions/borrowings. Short-term debt increased₹24.0073. Reclassifying that borrowing component gives−₹20.5959 operating cash before financing-classified interest. Less cash interest₹6.2541 and capex₹1.3101 gives−₹28.1601 cash after those items, before disposals/other investing/financing. This is an analytical reclassification shown alongside the original, not a claim of a fully repaired cash-flow statement. Parent FY26 adjusted CFO similarly−₹20.8169;FY25 parent₹23.6111 less₹21.9812 debt movement is₹1.6299. Weak CFO is explained by operating assets and classifications, not excused by capex, which belongs in investing cash. [S01, printed114–115/150–151, cash-flow statements; S20, corrected statements pp.9/18; E06/E08.]\\n\\nThe parent three-year as-filed ratio of summed CFO to summed PAT is-11.88%, not an average of yearly ratios. It is a diagnostic only: earlier MayFY24 results CFO−₹33.9131 differs from full annual-report/later comparative−₹33.7160. Original FY24 Note18 explicitly identifies₹25fixed deposit inside other current assets, resolving later cash₹25.1674 versus original₹0.1674 as a cash-definition reclassification, not missing cash. The₹25deposit placement also sits in original operating cash movement: analytically moving it to investing givesFY24 operatingCFO−₹8.716before interest, not−₹33.716. Combining that with borrowing-adjustedFY25/FY26 gives₹−27.903cash and-47.94%of summedPAT, still before financing-classified interest. This adjusted series remains an analytical diagnostic, not a certified restatement. FY23 cash-flow comparatives also differ from prospectus restatement. All vintages are retained separately. First-year group FY25 CFO starts zero cash and uses closing asset balances. Its+₹58.21 originally called changes on consolidation is relabelled purchase of fixed assets in the FY26 comparative, with the same positive sign. It is not valid negative capex, and no clean cumulative group cash-conversion ratio is asserted. [S19, FY24 results BS/CF; S26, printed90/101; S02, parent comparatives and PDF158 groupCF; S03, restatedCF; S01, comparativeCF; E06–E08/E22.]\\n\\n**Working capital and asset quality.** Group AR₹43.4239 fell from₹57.5240, but unbilled₹58 rose from₹18.1763 and inventory₹69.1812 from₹51.8392. AP₹37.5217 versus₹29.2270 only partly funds this. All₹43.4239 disclosed receivables are in6 month-plus buckets:₹29.3189 at6–12 months,₹9.9723 at1–2 years,₹2.2059 at2–3 years and₹1.9268 over3 years, with nil allowance. The ageing basis and collection evidence deserve direct verification; nil accounting provision is not proof of zero credit loss. Inventory consists₹48.4269 traded goods and₹20.7543 WIP, also with nil diminution provision. Obsolescence, acceptance delays and unbilled recoverability can impair both earnings and borrowing base. [S01, printed162–164/174, Notes15–19/38; E03–E04.]\\n\\n**Capital bridge.** Detailed groupONWC includes AR+unbilled+inventory+supplier advances/prepaids/government operating balances+commission receivable−AP−operating current liabilities; income-tax assets and accrued deposit interest are excluded. OperatingIC adds PPE/intangibles/CWIP, operating security and margin deposits. FinancingIC equals equity including warrant cash+NCI+debt−reported cash−nonoperating loan−investment. The difference is reconciled to tax assets, accrued interest, tax/gratuity provisions and deferred tax, with small source-rounding residual separately exposed. Historical parent broad proxies cannot provide this same reliable classification; their residuals are not hidden. ΔIC is cross-checked against capex−DA+ΔONWC+other operating investment. FY26 ₹18.096CWIP commissioning is a transfer, not new cash investment. Project and acquired-capital returns remain NS; a negative or distorted denominator is never celebrated as exceptional ROIC. [S01, printed148/160–165, Notes9–19; historical_metrics.json detailed calculations; E07/E08/E13.]\\n\\n**Funding.** Gross debt₹68.8823 includes overdrafts₹23.5518, invoice factoring₹32.2300, current term maturities₹9.4342, long-term debt₹3.6169 and related loan₹0.0494. Factoring is financing, not automatically collected customer cash. Reported groupcash₹27.4615 includes deposits₹27.1717; only₹0.2898 current accounts/cash is the conservative usable floor. Separate margin deposits₹2.4385 sit in other assets and are never added again. Collateral is linked to deposits; exact freedom by account isND, so all deposits are excluded in the main model. CRISIL23 September BBB-/Stable/A3, on a standalone approach, calls liquidity adequate, but discloses91.02% average bank-line use and367.2gross-current-asset days. Of₹125rated facilities,₹23.25is cash credit,₹58.20LC/BG,₹43.55 proposed funded facilities. Proposed lines and guarantees are not cash available to finance a shortfall. Its₹9.4 annual debt-obligation estimate and positive credit view are important contrary evidence. A computed₹2.08785unused-capacity proxy is expressly uncommitted and not anApril draw permission. [S01, Notes5/8/14/17/36; S17,23September rating rationale, liquidity/facility annexure; E12–E13.]\\n\\n**Opening booked obligations.** Model operating working capital excludes tax and long provisions, so they are not silently dropped: ₹6.4064opening tax is split into₹3.1594arrears paid in bridgepre7 and₹3.2470remaining booked tax paid atY1M03. Opening gratuity₹0.4941 is paid atY1M12. These are explicit timing assumptions, with sensitivities; no current tax-asset cash credit is taken. They are separate cash uses from expenses/tax on new earnings, tracked through period/annual columns and the remaining-obligation rollforward. The₹1.6190opening deferred-tax liability is not ordinary debt or asserted presently due: default separately reserves that amount in terminal cash; month12/24/60payment sensitivities replace, not duplicate, that reserve. Possible overlap with normalized future cash taxes makes this a conservative stress, not a precise tax valuation. [S01, printed159–160 Notes7/11 and printed169 Note33; model_inputs.json/model_engine.py; E32.]\\n\\n**Share/cash claims.** March issued22,937,688;24 August promoter conversion1,030,926 makes23,968,614;13 October issue1,950,000 at₹40.03 makes25,918,614 and₹7.80585gross proceeds. Older remaining2,061,856 warrants originally₹48.50 have₹36.375balance; new2,500,000 at₹40.03 have25%upfront₹2.501875 crore and75%future₹7.505625 crore. Warrants-only potential30,480,470 is not the historical EPS denominator. The101,338share movement is resolved: FY26 directors report confirms employee-option exercise at₹10 on10February2026, already included in March shares. FY25 wording mixes563,200plan capacity and506,668underlying shares; full remaining-grant/forfeiture details are unavailable. The2024plan vests1–5years and permits exercise within3years thereafter, with grant-specific strike not below₹10. Conservatively reserving the461,862remaining plan capacity produces30,942,332economic claims with all warrants, versus30,885,800using405,330remaining grant-derived shares. Neither is asserted actual issued/outstanding. The model gives no option-proceeds credit, separates issued shares from terminal economic claims, and sensitizes0/405,330/461,862. March warrant balance₹0.7732 versus cash-flow receipt₹3.75 remains unreconciled. [S01, printed82; S02, printed83; S27, PDF10–13; E30.] Dividend₹1, paid12 October to23 September holders, is a pre-entry company cash outflow, not income for a19 October buyer. Subsequent21 October conversion is excluded by cutoff. [S01, share-capital/warrant notes andCF; S21,24August allotment; S06,13October allotment; S22, terms; S07, dividend payment; E15/E28.]\\n\\n## 10. Valuation & Market Expectations\\n\\nIssued market cap is₹194.78crore. Headline groupP/E is11.99× on P&L PAT, or11.51× on the conflicting EPS/reserve PAT. EBIT less finance at25%tax gives diagnosticP/E14.30×; it does not certify owner earnings. EV uses gross debt less only usable cash, excluding the deposits, and is9.97× recurring EBITDA. This simplified EV diagnostic does not assign a market value to minority claims or net the₹1.0710nonoperating loan/₹0.0080investment, whose realization is unverified; negative book NCI−₹0.6130 is not treated as cash or an automatic reduction in claim value. It therefore is not a fully reconciled acquisition EV. Full dilution without adding future proceeds is disclosed as a claim-count diagnostic, not an EV bridge. There is no supportable unconditional entry-price range whileG2 is unresolved. [S09,19October close; S06/S21 share bridge; S01 earnings/debt/cash; historical_metrics.json valuation calculations.]\\n\\n| Assumption | Bear | Base | Bull |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\\n| Annual revenue growth |−5%|10%|18%|\\n| Operating EBIT margin |7.5%|12%|15%|\\n| Billed / unbilled days |120 /150|80 /105|65 /75|\\n| Inventory / payable days |190 /75|165 /90|135 /100|\\n| Demand-facility rollover |75%|100%|100%|\\n| Terminal nominal INR k / g |18% /0%|16% /3%|14% /4%|\\n\\n|Scenario / funding / claims|Status|First breach|Gross CAGR|Rescue shares|Rescue cash|\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n|bear/no_new_finance|ABSORBING_FIRST_BREACH|preentry/pre1|NS|0|0.00|\\n|bear/bounded_optional|ABSORBING_FIRST_BREACH|investment/Y1M02|NS|2286377|10.00|\\n|bear/bounded_optional/warrant_exercise|ABSORBING_FIRST_BREACH|investment/Y1M02|NS|2286377|10.00|\\n|base/no_new_finance|ABSORBING_FIRST_BREACH|preentry/pre1|NS|0|0.00|\\n|base/bounded_optional|ABSORBING_FIRST_BREACH|investment/Y1M06|NS|2286377|10.00|\\n|base/bounded_optional/warrant_exercise|ABSORBING_FIRST_BREACH|investment/Y1M06|NS|2286377|10.00|\\n|bull/no_new_finance|ABSORBING_FIRST_BREACH|preentry/pre1|NS|0|0.00|\\n|bull/bounded_optional|CONDITIONAL|None|13.65%|1174545|5.14|\\n|bull/bounded_optional/warrant_exercise|CONDITIONAL|None|11.04%|1174545|5.14|\\n\\nBoth base branches fail atY1M06, before even the first assumed old-warrant exercise can arrive. The explicitly paid opening tax liability brings the cash failure forward; later funding cannot cure it. Neither has an ordinary return. Bull gross CAGR is13.65% if warrants expire, but only11.04% with their exercise and dilution, below the15%hurdle before trading costs. The current quote is above both original strikes, so the no-exercise bull must not be selected as the expected outcome. The15%base-growth hurdle requires about24.33038%operating EBIT margin with warrant exercise, versus the reported recurring margin about12.17%.\\n\\nThese are **conditional funding diagnostics, not probability-weighted forecasts**. The no-new-finance branch fails in thepre-entry bridge under its conservative cash floor and supplier-before-collection order; this does not mean ROX actually defaulted inApril. It means a March balance sheet with₹0.2898free cash cannot establish an unassisted October starting state. Bounded rescue uses up to₹2.08785 new debt,₹10 crore net equity and3 million rescue shares, also constrained by40 million authorized shares after reserving known/warrant claims and461,862potential ESOP plan shares. Rescue issue price is40%below the reference quote with3%issue fee. Whole-share issuance rounds up the required amount, never creates fractional claims or an unlimited plug. All financing is counterfactual and uncommitted. New bank debt cannot redraw its ownyear5 bullet; lifetime draw capacity and facility closure are enforced.\\n\\nThe model starts31 March and traverses202 days to19 October, splitting periods at24 August conversion,12 October dividend and13 October allotment. It then simulates60 monthly investment periods plus12 monthly continuing-operation periods. Every month splits supplier/payroll outflow before collections into32cycles, with1/4/16/64/128cycle tests. Every event retains cash before/after, debt, shares and phase. Borrowing and principal financing are charged full-period ending-exposure interest; tax is conservatively based on pre-draw interest and therefore is not optimistically reduced for a new rescue. Minimum cash₹0.10 is tested on every event. First breach absorbs: no later rescue, recovery price or ordinary CAGR is assigned to a failed path.\\n\\nPending warrants cannot survive to a fictitiousyear5exercise. Default expiry paths assume no holder exercise and no future cash/dilution; because the market quote exceeds strikes, that is not a prudent expectation by itself. Separate headline exercise paths assume all old/new warrants voluntarily convert at legal monthly boundaries before their18 month expiries, issuing shares and receiving only the unpaid75%then. A future subscription cannot fix an earlier breach. The comparison prevents an apparently attractive no-exercise outcome from hiding likely dilution. The separate ESOP upper-plan claim overlay is included in terminal shares without pretending an exercise date or crediting any proceeds; it cannot fund a cash shortfall. All returns are before personal tax and gross of spread/brokerage/impact except named1/2.5/5%-each-side cost cases. Whole-lot capacity is independently restrictive.\\n\\n**Earned terminal.** ContinuingFCFF isNOPAT minus the larger of actual capex−DA+ΔONWC+additional operating deposits and the investment needed for terminalgrowth at15%incremental return. EV=FCFF/(k−g), withk>g and positiveFCFF required. A full operating year must survive without additional optional financing. The model reserves enoughyear5 cash for its worst intraperiod draw plus any unfunded incremental reinvestment requirement; the remaining opening-obligation reserve is also retained, and only excesscash is added. Debt is subtracted once, deposits remain excluded, and assumed99%owner attribution is stressed95/100% because NCI attribution is not reliably reconciled. No interim dividends are assumed, so100%of investor proceeds are terminal; this concentration is a major model risk, not a claimed present-value DCF target. Higherk/lowerg and lower-margin tests are the multiple-normalization equivalent.\\n\\n|Hurdle|Funding|Exercise|EBIT margin bracket|\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n|0.00%|no_new_finance|0|NO_FEASIBLE_SIGN_CHANGE|\\n|0.00%|no_new_finance|1|NO_FEASIBLE_SIGN_CHANGE|\\n|0.00%|bounded_optional|0|NO_FEASIBLE_SIGN_CHANGE|\\n|0.00%|bounded_optional|1|16.580831–16.580831%|\\n|12.00%|no_new_finance|0|NO_FEASIBLE_SIGN_CHANGE|\\n|12.00%|no_new_finance|1|NO_FEASIBLE_SIGN_CHANGE|\\n|12.00%|bounded_optional|0|20.818958–20.818958%|\\n|12.00%|bounded_optional|1|22.215544–22.215544%|\\n|15.00%|no_new_finance|0|NO_FEASIBLE_SIGN_CHANGE|\\n|15.00%|no_new_finance|1|NO_FEASIBLE_SIGN_CHANGE|\\n|15.00%|bounded_optional|0|22.399567–22.399567%|\\n|15.00%|bounded_optional|1|24.330381–24.330381%|\\n|18.00%|no_new_finance|0|NO_FEASIBLE_SIGN_CHANGE|\\n|18.00%|no_new_finance|1|NO_FEASIBLE_SIGN_CHANGE|\\n|18.00%|bounded_optional|0|24.443645–24.443645%|\\n|18.00%|bounded_optional|1|26.738716–26.738716%|\\n\\nEvery scan and bisection, successful or failed, is retained. There are449unique full cash paths and873labels after lossless deduplication, not only chosen endpoints. Root scans include0%price-implied break-even and12/15/18%hurdles, and cover4–30%EBIT margins with every other stated assumption fixed, and revenue-growth grids0–40%without an unwarranted continuity claim. A mathematical hurdle is not an achievable operating plan. Additional two-way matrices vary margin×terminalk and growth×unbilled days. One-way tests cover both cash-conversion assets, inventory/payables, rates, caps, rescue discount/fees, collateral release, rollover, maintenance, owner share, terminal reinvestment and warrant exercise. Model failures remain visible and never become zero-return observations in an average.\\n\\n**Execution.** All60 official sessions24 July–19 October were observed with positive traded value. Twenty-day mean/median turnover₹62.5264/₹38.1496 lakh;60 day₹35.23883/₹16.1884 lakh. The60 day median is the conservative capacity reference. A₹5 lakh notional rounds up tofive lots/8000 shares/₹6.012 lakh. At5%of conservative daily value, literal₹5 lakh takes6.18 theoretical days and whole-lot reference7.43; actual order constraints may be worse. Median33600 share volume permits0/1/2 whole lots per day at2/5/10%. Rolling-window lot capacity and censored exits are retained in liquidity.json, not replaced by fractional-lot execution. NSE defines ST as SME trade-for-trade, requiring delivery settlement rather than ordinary rolling-market netting. The dated security extract records a₹71.40–₹78.90daily range, approximately5%around the reference close. The historical10%→5%change row could not be retained as an exact primary response, so no asserted transition date is used. Neither that range nor a circuit print proves executable depth. The window contains52SM and8STsessions, including24 July and9–19 October. There is no verified spread/order-book snapshot or complete currentASM/GSM restriction notice. [S09,60dated bhavcopy rows and19October security master; S25, ST settlement; liquidity.json; E19/E24.]\\n\\n## 11. Bear Case & Permanent-Loss Path\\n\\nThe strongest bear chain is hardware/project growth → inventory and unbilled acceptance delays → ageing without provisions → reduced lender borrowing base and less supplier credit → expensive rescue equity or missed obligations → permanently diluted or impaired owner value. A loss of a large customer/OEM relationship can simultaneously reduce margin and slow collections. Deposits pledged to lenders may protect creditors without protecting common shareholders. Selling inventory at a haircut and releasing receivables are not free upside: they can reduce equity recovery and future revenue. Impairment risk is **High**, with uncertainty too large for a precise probability or reliable bear recovery price. [Analyst linked stress based on S01 ageing/inventory/credit notes and S03 concentration risks; E03/E04/E12/E17.]\\n\\nThe single decisive variable is **cash realization of the billed and unbilled balances under verified funding terms**. The strongest evidence against a wholly negative interpretation is the unmodified audit, CRISILadequate-liquidity conclusion, actual fresh equity and operational delivery centres. These support further investigation, not an automatic dismissal. Conversely, a low headlineP/E or temporary share-price rebound does not reconcile owner cash. Model failure is a conditional financing boundary, not an allegation that the issuer is insolvent. [S01, unmodified audits and cash/asset notes; S17, liquidity conclusion; S06/S21, actual allotments; scenario_summary.json.]\\n\\n## 12. 5× / 10× Feasibility\\n\\nFive-year5× requires37.97%annual share-price growth and₹375.75;10×58.49%and₹751.50. At30,942,332conservative economic claims including the remaining-plan ESOP overlay, these require about₹1163 crore/₹2325 crore equity, before any additional rescue dilution. Even a20×terminalP/E requires roughly₹58/₹116 crore owner earnings, and at8%owner margin approximately₹727/₹1453 crore revenue. A12×multiple raises required profits further. Exact arithmetic is retained in reverse_results.json. Those outcomes require multiplefold real economic expansion, funded working capital, attractive reinvestment, resolved accounting and controlled dilution. Neither a small market cap nor broad cloud TAM supplies that evidence. Classification: **Speculative / unsupported**, not a price target or a probability claim. [Calculated from S09 price and S06/S21/S22 claim counts; reverse_results.json outcome hurdles. Not guidance.]\\n\\n## 13. Monitoring Plan\\n\\n| KPI/event | Baseline | Improvement/milestone | Warning versus thesis break | Review/source |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Financial reconciliation | Borrowing embedded in CFO; owner PAT/EPS conflict | Signed line-by-line bridges to revised statements | Alert: incomplete response; break: substantiated material unreliability persists without remediation | Next audited/revised filing |\\n| Contract cash | Unbilled₹58, aged AR₹43.4239 | Acceptance dates and bank-reconciled subsequent collections | Alert: further growth above sales; break: material unrecoverable balances | Next results plus collection note |\\n| Actual liquidity | Usable floor₹0.2898, deposits₹27.1717 | Bank-confirmed free cash, lien schedule and committed undrawn lines | Alert: utilization remains near91%; break: actual unfunded due obligation | Next rating/financial update |\\n| Inventory |₹69.1812, WIP₹20.7543 | Ageing, turnover and cash-paid project completion | Alert: slower turns; break: material obsolete/unsupported inventory | Half-year/full-year notes |\\n| Service economics | Services/FMS₹16.3198 vs₹36.0863 | Paid recurring contracts, renewal/margin evidence | Alert: hardware-only sales growth; break: transition consumes capital without sustainable profit | Results and reconciled presentation |\\n| Capital deployment | CWIP commissioned, fresh preferential objects | Facility utilization and return on full capital including WC | Alert: timetable slips; break: persistent value destruction without credible correction | Proceeds/utilization filings |\\n| Warrants/claims | Warrants-only30,480,470; conservative ESOP-overlaid30,942,332 | Conversion cash/shares and expiry schedule reconcile | Alert: new dilutive proposal; break: unfair minority terms or unreconciled claims | Every allotment and shareholding filing |\\n| Governance/RPT | RP receivable₹7.1768; tax₹3.1594 arrears | Collections, arm's-length terms, cleared tax and reconciled subsidiary audit scope | Alert: balances grow; break: verified diversion/material concealment | Audit/RPT/tax disclosures |\\n| Tradeability | ST,1600lot,60 day median₹16.1884 lakh | Current restriction notice and executable depth | Alert: participation capacity falls; break: suspension/effectively no exit for intended size | Before any transaction |\\n\\nThese are research review triggers, not scheduled automations or universal mechanical sell rules. A missed quarter requires context; a documented integrity failure can change the gate immediately.\\n\\n## 14. Final Classification & Conditional Action\\n\\n**Pending evidence: Hold — unresolved. Research priority, not eligible for favourable new-investment classification.** The complete v3matrix cannot be applied to invented midpoint scores. All three composites remain NS; the record belongs in a separate pending-evidence table, not at the bottom of a numeric ranking. It does not meet compounder criteria because the required scores, cash resilience and critical-gate clearance are absent.\\n\\nA price decline alone cannot clearG2. Reconciled accounts plus independently verified collections/funding could allow rescoring; a supported, cash-funded base case meeting15%after realistic execution costs would then be required. If an existing holding exists, the relevant issue is reliability/funding/liquidity, not purchase-price anchoring. Position weights, tax basis and executable depth were not supplied, so no individualized exit count, allocation or trade is inferred. No security transaction is authorized by this research.\\n\\n## 15. Sources, Assumptions & Open Questions\\n\\nPrimary documents are linked below; material claims map to evidence IDs in evidence_ledger.json. Source dates and document hashes identify exactly what was read. Raw PDFs, OCR/extraction caches, private transfer helpers and Library identities are deliberately excluded from recovery archives. Authored numeric extracts preserve enough evidence, formulas and code to rebuild the full research offline; they are not claimed to replace independent reading of the linked originals.\\n\\n- S01: [FY2026 annual report](https://archives.nseindia.com/annual_reports/SME_AR_31858_ROXHITECH_2025_2026_A_3327582_08092026141331.pdf), 2026-09-08. Printed102–176: both full audit reports, KAMs, CARO, IFC, financial statements and notes; governance/statutory54–101; front-matter2–53. read primary locally.\\n- S02: [FY2025 annual report](https://archives.nseindia.com/annual_reports/SME_AR_28841_ROXHITECH_2024_2025_A_5416823_06092025204121.pdf), 2025-09-06. Printed104–176: audits/annexures, standalone118–145 and first consolidation154–176; fiscal2024 comparatives. read primary locally.\\n- S03: [IPO prospectus](https://www.rox.co.in/wp-content/uploads/investors/ROX%20-Prospectus_Final.pdf), 2023-11-13. Identity and risks pp1,23–27; business pp102–134; audited restated FY21–23 pp43–45 and F1–F45; capital, objects and RPT. read primary locally.\\n- S04: [May29 2025 earnings call transcript](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_03062025144422_intimationtranscript.pdf), 2025-06-03. pp7,13–16:20%growth aspiration, margins, receivables, project investment responses. read primary locally.\\n- S05: [June15 2026 earnings call transcript](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_18062026213513_intimationtranscript.pdf), 2026-06-18. pp2–13: NOC/SOC operational statement, seven digital transformation clients, financial and execution comments. read primary locally.\\n- S06: [October13 2026 allotment](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_13102026171735_Outcome_of_Board_meeting.pdf), 2026-10-13. pp1–2:1.95million new shares at40.03 and2.5million warrants; issued25,918,614 andfullydiluted30,480,470. read primary locally.\\n- S07: [Dividend completion](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_14102026170117_Press_release.pdf), 2026-10-14. p2:paymentOct12,recordSep23,Rs1/share,approx2.39crore. read primary locally.\\n- S08: [CRISIL rating assignment filing](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_05102026210601_Update.pdf), 2026-10-05. Rating letter and facility amounts. read primary locally.\\n- S10: [Independent director resignation](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_01102026193041_Reg_30_-_Independent_directro.pdf), 2026-10-01. Complete filing/annexures:resignation/noothermaterialreasons; no financial allegation established. read primary locally.\\n- S11: [FY26 investor presentation](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_08062026210312_investorpresentation.pdf), 2026-06-08. Customer concentration historicalFY25, positioning and FY24–26 financials. read primary locally.\\n- S12: [Dynacons FY26 annual report](https://www.dynacons.com/dynacons-annual-report-2025-26.pdf), FY2026 annual report; audit signed before cutoff. Consolidated financials and notes pp154–180; systemsintegration/managedservices. read primary locally.\\n- S13: [Dynacons FY26 presentation](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/DSSL_02062026122429_PRESENTATIONDSSLMARCH2026.pdf), 2026-06-02. pp9,23,35–36 revenue/margins/mix. read primary locally.\\n- S14: [Allied Digital FY26 presentation](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ADSL_26052026124043_CoveringLetterinvestorpresentation.pdf), 2026-05-26. pp30–36 financials,CFO,adjusted EBITDA andprovision caveat. read primary locally.\\n- S15: [Orient Technologies FY26 annual report](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/680b427b158e6c535e8eb95b/6a970274d84d48d87c12d85d_Orient%20India%20AR%202026-Final_compressed.pdf), FY2026; signed May27; available on issuer site by cutoff. Printed45 business performance;185–186 consolidated P&L and CF; segment and exceptional notes. read primary locally.\\n- S16: [Orient Q1FY27 presentation](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/680b427b158e6c535e8eb95b/6a7da53c0046e8df0a08bb12_Investor%20Presentation_Q1FY27_signed.pdf), 2026-08-12. Recent operating trajectory and economicmix. read primary locally.\\n- S09: [NSE dated daily market and security extracts](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/content/cm/BhavCopy_NSE_CM_0_0_0_20261019_F_0000.csv.zip), 2026-10-19. ROXHITECH/INE0PDJ01013 rows; full60dated-source provenance in market_extract.json and security_extract.json. read and verified primary.\\n- S17: [CRISIL ROX detailed rating rationale](https://www.crisil.com/mnt/winshare/Ratings/RatingList/RatingDocs/ROXHi_TechLimited_September%2023_%202026_RR_405556.html), 2026-09-23. Analytical approach, strengths/weaknesses, liquidity and bank-facility annexures. read primary with web; local406; no copiedrawHTML required.\\n- S18: [Allied Digital CRISIL rationale](https://www.crisilratings.com/mnt/winshare/Ratings/RatingList/RatingDocs/AlliedDigitalServicesLimited_October%2001_%202025_RR_371630.html), 2025-10-01. GCA/receivables/provision/liquidity/financials and consolidation scope. read primary; historical comparison not currentrating assertion.\\n- S19: [Original FY24 audited annual results](https://www.rox.co.in/wp-content/uploads/investors/Financial%20results2425.pdf), 2024-05-30. Complete annual-results audit and financial statements; results filing alone does not contain full CARO/IFC; see recovered S26. read primary locally.\\n- S20: [July15 corrected FY26 results and auditor reports](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_15072026131754_Clarifiaction_Letter.pdf), 2026-07-15. 19 pages: revision cover, June30 responses, both audit reports and statements. read primary locally.\\n- S21: [August24 promoter warrant conversion](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_24082026183951_Allotment_Outcome24082026.pdf), 2026-08-24. Full filing:1,030,926 shares, paid-up23,968,614. read primary locally.\\n- S22: [July25 EGM notice filed July29](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_29072026155954_NSE_-_EGM.pdf), 2026-07-29. Items1–2, funding objects,25/75% warrant terms,18month expiry and dilution table. read primary locally.\\n- S23: [Beneficial-owner clarification](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_31082026113259_Reg_30_Intimation.pdf), 2026-08-31. UBO changes from not applicable to Aditya Bhutra and Ankita Rathi. read primary locally.\\n- S24: [Investor-name clarification](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_13102026155428_Reg_30.pdf), 2026-10-13. Ray Invest corrected to Raynvvest; other terms unchanged. read primary locally.\\n- S25: [NSE SME market sub-segments](https://www.nseindia.com/static/products-services/emerge-sme-market-segment), Current official market rules read at research; issuer series dated19October2026. ST trade-for-trade settlement and standard lots. read primary with web.\\n- S26: [Original FY24 full annual report and AGM notice](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROXHITECH_31082024163244_AGMnotice.pdf), 2024-08-31. PDF41–45 full audit/CARO/IFC; PDF47 cashflow; printed101 Note18 FD25; printed104 Note27 historical Ingram proceeding. read primary locally.\\n- S27: [ROX Employee Stock Option Plan2024 EGM notice](https://www.rox.co.in/wp-content/uploads/investors/Rox%20-%20EGM%20Notice%20-%204-3-2024%20Final.pdf), 2024-02-28. PDF1–2 resolutions;10–13 plan ceiling, vesting, pricing, exercise and accounting. read primary locally.\\n- S28: [FY2023 AGM notice and directors report only](https://www.rox.co.in/wp-content/uploads/investors/Annual%20report%20202223.pdf), 2023-08-24. 18pages, notice dated24August/directors report21July; PDF7 highlights, PDF12–14 auditor discussion; actual audit/annexures not included. complete18-page file read; not a full audit report.\\n\\n**Priority unresolved questions:** reconcile remaining CFO/debt vintages; the FY24₹25FD cash-definition change is explained; explain+₹58.21consolidation/fixed-asset line; reconcile₹9.3501unbilled difference and subsidiary audit scope; bridge owner PAT/exceptional/EPS; verify individual deposit liens and current drawable facilities; show post-yearend collections and provisions; reconcile RPT service amounts and receivables; reconcile March warrantcash and remaining ESOP grants/forfeitures/strikes; quantify actual proceeds deployment, current customer/vendor concentration and post-allotment promoter encumbrance. FY24 full annual audit annexures were recovered and inspected; Original FY21/FY22/FY23 full annual audit reports were not independently retrieved or represented as inspected. The recovered18-page FY23 file is notice/directors material only, despite referring to an annexed audit. [S28, entire file.] The prospectus examiner reports reliance on prior FY21/FY22 auditor reports and presents audited restatedFY21–23 schedules; that is distinct from independently inspecting the originalFY23full audit and annexures. [S03, restatement examiner report F1–F3.] These are explicit research limits, not silently passed checks.\\n\\nCalculation conventions: closing working-capital days use revenue for billed/unbilled and product cost for inventory/payables, labelled accordingly. Revenue less product cost is a value-added proxy before labour and other delivery costs, not a verified segment gross margin. Normal tax25%, cost-of-capital13–17%, scenario capital intensity and rescue terms are analyst assumptions. Historical cash capex is gross purchase outflow, not netdisposals; capital transfers are not cashcapex. CF borrowing reclassification and financing-interest adjustment are shown separately. Group and parent are never spliced. No probabilities, unverified peer multiples, exact market share, invented quarterly CFO or unqualified fair value are supplied.\\n\\n**Update log.** Initial20 October2026cutoff assessment uses19 Octprice. Primary July15revisions, original FY24results/full annual audit, ESOP2024scheme, Augustconversion and JulyEGM terms were recovered during this research and incorporated before freeze. These improve evidence coverage but do not clearG2. The model was corrected before freeze to charge intraperiod rescue interest, close borrowing at maturity, expire warrants inside their legal horizon, date known pre-entry cash flows, reserve potential ESOP claims and separate the resolved FY24FD cash reclassification from still-unresolved group cash flows, and explicitly settle/reserve opening tax and gratuity obligations before calculating equity returns. These are methodology/implementation corrections, not subsequent issuer events or a manufactured score change.\\n\\n**All 16 v3 final checks:**\\n1. Identity/security/scope/date verified and explicit.\\n2. Material primary records read; management/analyst statements labelled; unavailable originals disclosed.\\n3. Audit/RPT/funding/dilution reviewed with proportionate gates, no fraud inference.\\n4. Units and periods separated; original/comparative vintages retained; no overlappingTTM.\\n5. Revenue growth separated from invoice mix, unbilled recognition and perimeter; organic unknown remains NS.\\n6. CFO/PAT uses summed numerator/denominator; capex does not excuse weak CFO; ratio comparability caveat retained.\\n7. Incremental-return numerator, fullcapital denominator, timing, residual and project IRR limitations visible.\\n8. Normalization, rent/leases, tax, NCI and dated dilution consistent and sensitized; unresolved owner PAT not hidden.\\n9. Every scenario links pre-entry/intraperiod cash, financing, reinvestment and terminal reserve; failure absorbs.\\n10. All13 canonical factors reused exactly; each composite's weights sum100%.\\n11. Missing evidence stays NS with coverage and mathematical bounds; no renormalization.\\n12. Raw/final scores reconcile; only explicit governance/funding/growth-quality overrides tested.\\n13. Classification follows gate-first rules; no unsupported compounder designation.\\n14. ₹5 lakh plus roundedwhole-lot position assessed; quote/turnover not promised execution.\\n15. Strongest bear, contrary evidence and cash-realization thesis-break variable explicit.\\n16. Samev3cutoff/tie rules apply; pending record visibly unranked, not batch-complete or a winner.\\n\\nCheck completion means the requirement was addressed, not that missing evidence is resolved. Both compact and full recovery packages must rebuild generated outputs after those outputs and attestations are removed under an offline declared-input guard. Independent verification is recorded separately and cannot be inherited from a copied badge.\\n\"","\"number\"","\"content_markdown\"","\"Executive Verdict\"","\"\\n**Hold — unresolved financial reliability. BQS NS; GQS NS; IAS NS.** ROX sells and integrates enterprise IT hardware, software and support, with an emerging managed-services proposition. Its two-decade operating history, OEM relationships and newly operational delivery facilities provide a credible business opportunity, but do not establish proprietary software economics. FY26 invoiced revenue shifted toward products while services contracted. More importantly, reported operating cash includes borrowing movements, the consolidated comparative cash-flow construction is not comparable, unbilled revenue and profit/share reconciliations remain unresolved, and most reported cash is in deposits linked to credit facilities. These are specific verification problems despite unmodified audit opinions, not a fraud finding. At ₹75.15 on 19 October 2026, a roughly 194.78crore issued-share valuation cannot be called attractive from the headline 11.99× P/E. This is a funding-sensitive integration/managed-services transition to investigate, not an evidence-backed compounder. Reconciled accounts, collected contract assets and independently verified available liquidity, rather than a lower quote alone, would change the conclusion. [S01, printed148–175, Notes17–20/30/32; S09; E02–E15.]\\n\\n\"","\"Research Header, Gates and Data Confidence\"","\"\\n- Exact issuer: ROX Hi-Tech Limited, formerly ROX Trading and Systems Private Limited. NSE ROXHITECH; ISIN INE0PDJ01013; CIN L51506TN2002PLC048598. Indian Accounting Standards under Indian GAAP/AS, not assumed Ind AS. Incorporation March2002 is not confused with November2023 listing. [S01, Notes1–2; S03, cover/general information; S09 security row.]\\n- Information cutoff:20 October2026. Market observation:19 October2026 close₹75.15, last₹75.00; not a live executable offer. All monetary financial tables below are ₹crore unless expressly labelled otherwise.\\n- Current issued claims:25,918,614 after13 October allotment. The dated security master still shows23,968,614, a lag explicitly overridden by the primary allotment. Warrants-only potential claims30,480,470 include2,061,856 older and2,500,000 new warrants, before separate ESOP uncertainty. The conservative remaining-plan overlay461,862 gives30,942,332 total economic claims, not actual issued shares. Weighted historical EPS denominators are different. [S06, pp.1–2; S21, p.1; S22, warrant terms/dilution table.]\\n- Latest annual financials:FY26; parent historical series FY21–26 and separately FY25–26 group. No invented quarterly/H1FY27 cash flow and no overlapping TTM. Horizonfive years, nominal INR equity hurdle15%, sensitivities12/18%; ₹5 lakh illustrative position, not a supplied user holding.\\n- Confidence: High on identity, source wording, observed daily turnover and allotments; Medium on business positioning and execution statements; Low on normalized owner earnings, underlying organic growth, comparable cash and incremental returns. An audited label does not eliminate contradictory audited schedules.\\n\\n| Gate | Finding | Consequence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| G1 governance | Hold — unresolved stewardship/reporting and RPT reconciliation; no substantiated diversion or severe minority harm | GOV NS, no unsupported governance-fraud override |\\n| G2 financial reliability | Hold — unresolved material cash-flow, contract-asset, consolidated-scope and profit/EPS issues | IAS NS and no favourable new-entry classification |\\n| G3 funding/survival | Conditional: no reported default, but near-full limits and large working-capital assets | Conditional stress only; an assumed model breach is not proof of actual default |\\n| G4 tradability | Conditional: 1600 share lot, observed ST series, limited participation and incomplete restriction/depth evidence | Not suspended or automatically untradeable; practical exit limits remain |\\n\\n\"","\"Scorecard and Calculation Audit\"","\"\\n|Factor|Score|Confidence|Evidence and reason|\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n|GOV|NS|Low|E05, E11, E14, E15, E23: Stewardship not scoreable until repeated reporting, RPT and capital reconciliation issues resolve.|\\n|MOAT|4|Medium|E02, E17, E20: Relationships, OEM certifications and integrated delivery are useful but contestable; gross hardware economics dominate disclosed invoicing.|\\n|REV|NS|Low|E02, E03, E16, E22: Gross reported3/5year growth can be calculated but material unbilled/perimeter and product/service changes obstruct reliable underlying expansion.|\\n|DUR|5|Medium|E02, E16, E17: Cloud, security, enterprise modernisation and installed-client cross-sell form accessible avenues; public orderbook lacks cash/margin reconciliation.|\\n|CAP|NS|Low|E07, E08, E09, E13: Incremental capital proxy exposed but unresolved cash, consolidation and profit bridges make reliable score unavailable.|\\n|CASH|3|Medium|E03, E04, E06, E08, E22: Persistent debt-funded working capital, aged balances and weak borrowing-adjusted cash are material recurring weaknesses.|\\n|BAL|NS|Low|E11, E12, E13, E15: Large restricted deposits, near-full lines, uncertain current cash and recent financing prevent reliable survival score.|\\n|EXEC|4|Medium|E16, E03, E13: FY26 missed stated20%growth aspiration; promised WC reduction not achieved on combined metrics.|\\n|EARN|NS|Low|E09, E10, E15: Conflicting profit/EPS and changing dilution obstruct dependable per-share recurring earnings scoring.|\\n|R|NS|Low|E09, E18: Conditional paths do not underwrite a probability-weighted expected return.|\\n|D|NS|Low|E12, E13, E18: Survival depends on actual drawablecash,collectionsandrefinancingstillunverified.|\\n|P|NS|Low|E09, E15, E18: Reverse thresholds computed but unreliablebasecannotestablishattractiveness.|\\n|L|4|Medium|E19, E24: Starting5from5–10days;explicitonepointdeductionfor1600-sharelotandST/circuitconstraints.|\\n\\n|Composite|Known contribution|Coverage|Exact raw bounds|Cap|Final|Post-cap display bounds|\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n|BQS|1.92|48.00%|2.44–7.12|None|NS|2.4–7.1|\\n|GQS|1.30|30.00%|2.00–8.30|5|NS|2.0–5.0|\\n|IAS|0.40|10.00%|1.6600–8.6800|None|NS|1.7–8.7|\\n\\nWeights are unchanged from the recovered v3.0 master. BQS: GOV20%, MOAT20%, REV12%, DUR10%, CAP12%, CASH10%, BAL8%, EXEC8%. Known contributions are0.80+0.50+0.30+0.32=1.92, covering48%. GQS: REV40%, DUR20%, EARN15%, CAP15%, CASH10%; known1.00+0.30=1.30, covering30%. IAS: exact final BQS25%, R35%, D20%, P10%, L10%; onlyL contributes0.40, covering10%. Nested BQS bounds are propagated, never substituted as a midpoint or as a score.\\n\\nPersistent poor cash realization supports CASH3 and the stated GQS cap5. The aggregate remains **NS**, not5. No governance or funding cap is silently applied merely because evidence is missing. Missing-factor bounds are mathematical possibilities, not statistical intervals or a ranking. Exact unrounded Decimal arithmetic and all contributions are in scores.json. Moving MOAT4 by±1 changes BQS bounds by±0.20 and IAS bounds by±0.05; moving DUR5 by±1 changes BQS bounds by±0.10, GQS by±0.20 and IAS by±0.025. These uncertain known judgments do not cure the missing critical factors. Boundary tests separately exercise GOV3/4, G1/G3 failure, G2 hold, NS with caps and persistent versus transient capital problems.\\n\\nL starts at5 for approximately5–10 theoretical participation days; one disclosed point is deducted for large lot/ST/circuit/depth constraints. No extra liquidity penalty is subsequently added to IAS.\\n\\n\"","\"Business Overview\"","\"\\nROX sources enterprise IT products and software, designs and installs infrastructure, and provides support, facilities management, cybersecurity, cloud, digital transformation and application services. OEM/channel relationships include IBM, Cisco and SAP. These relationships help sell complex projects but the OEM normally owns the underlying technology. Customer logos and partner awards are not proof of exclusive supply rights, intellectual property, subscription retention or pricing power. No independently reconciled ARR, software retention/cohorts, licensed-IP gross margin or SaaS unit economics is available. [S03, business section pp.102–134; S11, business/partner slides; E01–E02.]\\n\\nFY26 consolidated operating revenue₹202.9826 comprises invoiced products/services₹172.5090 plus a P&L unbilled-revenue contribution₹30.4736. Invoices comprise domestic products₹151.8876, SEZ products₹4.3016, services₹16.0432 and FMS₹0.2766. Product invoicing is90.54% of invoices, not a disclosed90.54% of final total recognized revenue because the unbilled component has no comparable product/service split. FY25 services/FMS were₹36.0863 and products₹123.8447. Therefore a blanket IT-services valuation ignores the actual disclosed mix. Product resale can create large gross sales with modest retained value, while integration projects tie cash in inventory, acceptance milestones and unbilled work. Recurring support can be better economics, but its revenue and capital returns have not been separately demonstrated. [S01, printed164, Note20; E02–E03.]\\n\\nThe business has Indian enterprise customers plus overseas subsidiaries. Consolidation begins only FY25; a two-year group comparison is not a five-year organic history. Overseas audit reliance is discussed below. Commissioning a50-seat facility is potential delivery capacity, not proof of utilization, paid seats or revenue per employee. [S01, subsidiary and audit other-matter disclosures, printed141–147; S02, PDF151/155; S05, operating update.]\\n\\n\"","\"Moat / Industry Position\"","\"\\n| Proposed mechanism | Supporting evidence | Durability test and failure mode |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Installed-customer knowledge and integrated delivery | Long operating record, OEM certifications, broad project capability | Renewal/retention and service contribution ND; capable integrators can compete; OEMs retain technology bargaining power |\\n| Technical qualification and execution | SAP/IBM/Cisco positioning; management reports NOC/SOC live and clients onboard | Certifications are renewable and not exclusive; people can leave, new systems displace old expertise |\\n| Scale/cross-sell | Existing enterprise relationships and management-reported new transformation clients | Must produce cash-paid higher-value services rather than more low-retained-value hardware |\\n| Customer switching costs | Integration effort can make disruption costly | Purchase-order contracting and multiple supplier options weaken contractual lock-in; no quantified switching-cost evidence |\\n\\nProspectus FY23 top10 customers were46.68% of sales and top5 approximately41.45%; the FY26 presentation shows historical FY25 top10 at35%. That is useful reported diversification, but current FY26 top10 and vendor concentration percentages are ND. Contracts are generally purchase-order based, without broad long-term customer volume guarantees; the prospectus discloses no fixed vendor pricing or automatic pass-through protection. More customers do not establish low dependence on particular OEMs or a small number of large projects.\\n\\n**Named economic peers, primary-source comparison.** Dynacons Systems & Solutions, Orient Technologies and Allied Digital are relevant integration/managed-services comparisons, not interchangeable valuation twins. Dynacons FY26 consolidated revenue₹1424.2834, total PAT₹84.8124, owner PAT₹84.7352 and CFO₹46.1345 versus₹66.0423 prior demonstrate greater scale but uneven cash. Its₹155.3178 lease liabilities and₹29.9084 lease cash payments complicate an asset-light EBITDA comparison. Its presentation shows data-centre34%, networking12%, workplace31% and managed-services23% mix. Orient FY26 revenue₹869.5445, reported EBITDA includingOI₹49.1473 and owner PAT₹4.5700 reflect₹23.6833 exceptional expenses: discontinued-customer costs roughly₹19.60 and labour-code liability₹4.08. CFO is−₹19.4101 and capex₹63.0047. The ₹19.5989customer-discontinuation write-off is an economic execution/capitalization loss even when labelled exceptional. Its solutions₹418.3724 versus services₹451.1721 mix and revised segment reporting are more informative than a single P/E. Allied FY26 presentation reports roughly₹968 revenue and adjusted EBITDA₹112 includingOI, explicitly excluding₹36 provision; CFO−₹78.52 versus₹92.27 is a warning, not evidence of clean sector cash generation. Its older CRISIL rationale describes lengthy working capital and an ECL provision. Peer strengths and weaknesses support skepticism of gross-sales multiples and unadjusted EBITDA, not a mechanically assigned premium or a claim that all peers are superior. No current peer trading multiple is invented. [S12, PDF154–157; S13, slides9/23/35–36; S15, printed45/185–186, Note33; S14, slides34–36; S18, working-capital/rating rationale; E20/E21/E25.]\\n\\n\"","\"Revenue Growth & Scale\"","\"\\n|Window|Endpoints revenue|Reported CAGR|ΔNOPAT|Δbroad IC|Diagnostic ΔNOPAT/ΔIC|Capital/investment residual|\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n|2023–2026|133.33 → 207.92|15.97%|2.48|128.71|1.93%|-0.04|\\n|2021–2026|64.07 → 207.92|26.55%|18.88|165.08|11.43%|-0.15|\\n\\nSources/calculation: [S01/S02/S03; historical_metrics.json, windows.] Ten-year revenue CAGR is unavailable because a comparableFY16endpoint was not retrieved; no backfilled estimate is supplied.\\n\\nThe reported parent sequence₹64.0718,102.8622,133.3279,176.0586,186.5068,207.9243 shows real commercial scaling worth investigating, including annual rupee additions₹38.7904,30.4657,42.7307,10.4482 and21.4175. It is not penalized merely for starting small. FY21, however, is a pandemic-affected low base, and later unbilled recognition and group formation distort a simple organic-CAGR interpretation. Group FY26 revenue grew8.28%, versus parent11.48%; parent and group must not be spliced. [S03, restated financials pp.43–45/F1 onward; S02, FY24 comparatives; S01, parent and group P&L; historical_inputs.json.]\\n\\nThe FY25–26 invoiced bridge is products+₹32.3445, services/FMS−₹19.7665, giving invoice growth₹12.5780 or7.86%. The additional unbilled P&L contribution increased₹2.9472. Recognized group sales rose₹15.5252. This bridge identifies product/service mix, not units, prices or customer-level organic volume. FX, acquisitions, like-for-like customer gains/losses and price/volume are not separately reconciled. In particular, unbilled balance grew₹39.8237, but P&L says₹30.4736: the₹9.3501 bridge is unresolved and matches a prior subsidiary-sales number. That numerical coincidence is a reconciliation question, not proof of fabrication. REV remains NS until genuine underlying expansion can be measured reliably. [S01, printed163–164, Notes19–20; E02–E03; calculated bridge in historical_metrics.json.]\\n\\n\"","\"Growth Quality & Reinvestment Runway\"","\"\\nDemand for modernization, cloud, data centres, cyber controls and enterprise applications offers accessible work through existing customer relationships. The useful bottom-up question is the number of funded, accepted and collected projects plus paid service contracts, not a global IT-spending TAM. Management reports seven new digital-transformation clients, a live NOC/SOC and a50-seat Trichy SEZ centre; contracted recurring revenue, utilization, unit pricing and customer profitability remain ND. No unsupported claim of capacity-limited exponential SaaS growth is made. [S05, June15 call pp.2–13; S11, delivery-capacity slides; E16.]\\n\\nThe model therefore uses explicit revenue, operating-margin and cash-day assumptions rather than fabricated customer counts. Base revenue grows10% annually from an8% above FY26 bridge run rate; bull18%; bear−5%. These are analyst scenarios, not guidance. Every incremental rupee requires inventory, receivables/contract assets, supplier credit, opex, cash taxes, maintenance and growth capex. A separate₹4.4571 security/margin-deposit bucket scales with the revenue run rate, with additional deposits paid in cash and no assumed release on contraction. The0/1/2×deposit-intensity sensitivities test that requirement. Maintenance is estimated at1.5% of revenue, stressed1–2%; incremental fixed investment5% of revenue additions is an assumption, not a disclosed project budget. A revenue/fixed-asset capacity ceiling10× prevents unlimited revenue with no assets, but is not evidence of actual capacity. Failure to obtain paid-seat/project economics keeps CAP/DUR confidence constrained. [Analyst assumptions: model_inputs.json/model_engine.py; S01, Note14 deposits.]\\n\\nParent broad invested-capital proxies and3/5 year changes are exposed above; they include CWIP and operating balances, not merely cash capex. They are accounting diagnostics with unresolved classification/perimeter bridges, not project IRRs. FY26 consolidated operating IC, separately reconstructed from detailed notes, is about₹177.71 versus₹134.50 prior; its NOPAT fell, so current additional capital has not yet demonstrated attractive returns. A13–17% nominal INR cost-of-capital range is a judgment for leveraged, illiquid integration economics, not a universal WACC. Terminal scenarios use14–18% with wider13/20% tests and explicitly fund sustainable growth at an assumed15% incremental return. Commissioned facilities may require a lag, but the report does not assume their eventual profit rescues poor observed returns. GQS remains NS with a5cap on its bound due to persistent cash weakness. [S01, printed148–165, Notes5–19; S02/S03 historical statements; historical_metrics.json, capital bridges; E07–E13.]\\n\\n\"","\"Management, Governance & Execution\"","\"\\nJim Rakesh and Sukanya Rakesh are the principal promoter/managing leadership. A long operating history and promoter ownership can align incentives but do not replace minority-owner cash outcomes. FY26 RPT service sales are₹4.3637 versus₹1.0249, related receivables₹7.1768 versus₹2.2467 and payables₹1.3238 versus₹3.6708. KMP remuneration₹1.3125 plus sitting fees₹0.1460 is disclosed; the standalone related-party service note₹5.4039 conflicts with its revenue note₹4.3637. Commercial related-party activity is not automatically abusive, but collectability, pricing and scope need reconciliation. Current promoter encumbrance and post-allotment free float are not fully verified, so neither a zero-pledge assertion nor a precise current promoter percentage is manufactured. [S03, promoter background; S01, printed167–168, Note30 and standalone Note20/30; E14.]\\n\\n| Dated statement/action | Observable outcome by cutoff | Assessment |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| May29,2025 call: around20% growth expectation and working-capital reduction | FY26 parent11.48%, group8.28%; billed AR fell, but billed+unbilled and inventory rose | Growth expectation missed; narrow debtor decline is not total cash improvement |\\n| June15,2026 call: NOC/SOC operational, clients onboard, seven transformation additions | Management reports commercialization and50-seat office; audited FY26 mix still hardware-heavy | Positive commissioning evidence; recurring economics not yet verified |\\n| IPO capital for delivery infrastructure and working capital | FY25 CWIP₹18.096 moves into FY26 computer/software assets; large operating asset expansion | Transfer is not equivalent to new FY26 cash capex or proof of returns |\\n| July25 EGM preferential proposal | Oct13 shares/warrants allotted; intended₹9.01 new business,₹4.50WC,₹4.50general purposes bySep2028 | Future warrant subscription is optional; objects are not actual use-of-proceeds evidence |\\n| May29 and July15 corrections after exchange queries | Revised results and later AR still retain identified CF ambiguities | Responding is positive; material bridges remain unresolved |\\n\\nThe18-page FY23 issuer file contains AGM/directors material but no actual audit/annexures. It reports Sundaresan & Subramanian resignation24April2023, L U Krishnan appointment and resignation29June citing preoccupation, then same-day P P N appointment. This management-disclosed chronology is not evidence of adverse outgoing findings. Its FY23/FY22 PAT₹15.3971/₹1.5409 differs from prospectus-restated₹15.3297/₹1.5131; revenue matches, and profit vintages remain separate. [S28, PDF7/12–14; S03, restated statements; E31.]\\n\\nFY24 original annual-results audit byPPN & Company is unmodified. After two damaged downloads, a readable official AGM/full annual-report copy was recovered. Its complete audit, CARO and IFC were inspected: unmodified opinion, affirmative IFC, positive audit trail, bank returns agreeing with books and no reported default, fraud or resignation. FY24 Note27 records a historical₹3.5939crore Ingram Micro cheque-bounce proceeding, with principal discharged but petition disposal awaited. Later contingent-claim notes are nil; court closure was not independently established. This is not current unpaid principal or a fraud finding. The pending charge on a₹11.60lakh vehicle loan is minor compliance context. [S26, PDF41–45 and printed100/104–105, Notes10/27; S01/S02, Note25.] FY25 and FY26 complete parent/group audit reports, KAMs, CARO, IFC and financial notes were inspected. FY25 CARO says an auditor resigned during the year without outgoing concerns; do not treat that statement as misconduct. FY26 Krishaan &Co opinions/IFC are unmodified/affirmative. KAMs focus on inventory, receivables and payables; only some confirmations are received and book balances are adopted for others. Subsidiaries are management-certified: FY25 audit literally describes assets₹10.9839/revenue₹10.3006, FY26 ₹0.2356/₹0.0880, an unresolved scope/unit contraction despite continuing entities. Group IFC conclusions likewise rely on management certificates. [S19, complete results audit; S26, full audit/CARO/IFC and historical litigation; S02, PDF107–117/151–155; S01, printed102–111/140–147; E05/E22/E27.]\\n\\nFY26 parent CARO records₹3.1594 FY25 self-assessment tax outstanding more than six months; group CARO says no adverse remarks, requiring reconciliation. No loan default or fraud is reported. The1 October independent-director resignation states no other material reasons and is not treated as proof of an audit dispute. JulyEGM beneficial-owner details were subsequently corrected from not applicable to named individuals, and investor nameRay Invest toRaynvvest. Disclosure corrections merit verification, not an unsupported allegation of hidden ownership.\\n\\n\"","\"Financial Forensics\"","\"\\n|FY standalone|Revenue|EBITDA ex OI|EBIT ex OI|PAT|CFO as filed|Cash capex|Reported FCF|Debt|Reported cash|Broad IC proxy|\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n|2021|64.07|1.07|0.92|0.66|3.15|1.11|2.04|11.35|3.37|15.69|\\n|2022|102.86|4.15|3.93|1.51|-4.87|0.20|-5.07|17.95|1.49|25.99|\\n|2023|133.33|23.02|22.78|15.33|3.73|0.69|3.04|22.58|0.01|52.06|\\n|2024|176.06|31.79|31.10|21.24|-33.72|7.97|-41.69|21.29|25.17|97.02|\\n|2025|186.51|28.52|27.47|19.32|23.61|22.89|0.72|46.58|27.45|135.98|\\n|2026|207.92|27.80|26.09|17.64|3.19|1.31|1.88|68.88|27.24|180.77|\\n\\nSources: [S03, prospectus restatementFY21–23; S02, FY24comparatives; S01, FY25–26parent; S19, originalFY24vintage separately. Exact figures/source IDs in historical_inputs.json.]\\n\\n**Cash is not simply PAT less capex.** FY26 consolidated revenue₹202.9826 less product cost₹150.0922, employee₹15.9058 and other operating expense₹10.5776 gives recurring EBITDA₹26.4070 and EBIT₹24.7016 afterDA₹1.7054. Printed EBITDA₹29.1156 includesOI₹2.7086. Finance expense₹6.5464 and taxes then affect owner earnings. P&L PAT₹16.2435, EPS/reserve-linked₹16.9275 and directors' summary₹16.19 are not a single verified normalized owner numerator. The₹0.6840 exceptional line and EPS differences7.11/7.37 versus7.41/7.38 remain open. A simple EBIT less finance, taxed25%, is only a diagnostic, not an audit reconciliation. Stock-option compensation expense and its cash-flow addback are not separately reconciled, so no SBC addback is made to normalized profit or owner cash. The conservative claim overlay captures dilution, not a claim that employee compensation is free. [S27, PDF13 accounting policy; S01, printed82 and expense notes.] Rent₹1.8496 is already in opex; do not add a second rental deduction or manufacture IndAS lease debt. The asset schedule includes a leasing-asset line but does not establish an omitted quantified lease liability. [S01, printed149/157/164–168, P&L and Notes20–24/32; E09–E10.]\\n\\nFY26 as-filed group CFO₹3.4114 includes₹25.4567 labelled short-term provisions/borrowings. Short-term debt increased₹24.0073. Reclassifying that borrowing component gives−₹20.5959 operating cash before financing-classified interest. Less cash interest₹6.2541 and capex₹1.3101 gives−₹28.1601 cash after those items, before disposals/other investing/financing. This is an analytical reclassification shown alongside the original, not a claim of a fully repaired cash-flow statement. Parent FY26 adjusted CFO similarly−₹20.8169;FY25 parent₹23.6111 less₹21.9812 debt movement is₹1.6299. Weak CFO is explained by operating assets and classifications, not excused by capex, which belongs in investing cash. [S01, printed114–115/150–151, cash-flow statements; S20, corrected statements pp.9/18; E06/E08.]\\n\\nThe parent three-year as-filed ratio of summed CFO to summed PAT is-11.88%, not an average of yearly ratios. It is a diagnostic only: earlier MayFY24 results CFO−₹33.9131 differs from full annual-report/later comparative−₹33.7160. Original FY24 Note18 explicitly identifies₹25fixed deposit inside other current assets, resolving later cash₹25.1674 versus original₹0.1674 as a cash-definition reclassification, not missing cash. The₹25deposit placement also sits in original operating cash movement: analytically moving it to investing givesFY24 operatingCFO−₹8.716before interest, not−₹33.716. Combining that with borrowing-adjustedFY25/FY26 gives₹−27.903cash and-47.94%of summedPAT, still before financing-classified interest. This adjusted series remains an analytical diagnostic, not a certified restatement. FY23 cash-flow comparatives also differ from prospectus restatement. All vintages are retained separately. First-year group FY25 CFO starts zero cash and uses closing asset balances. Its+₹58.21 originally called changes on consolidation is relabelled purchase of fixed assets in the FY26 comparative, with the same positive sign. It is not valid negative capex, and no clean cumulative group cash-conversion ratio is asserted. [S19, FY24 results BS/CF; S26, printed90/101; S02, parent comparatives and PDF158 groupCF; S03, restatedCF; S01, comparativeCF; E06–E08/E22.]\\n\\n**Working capital and asset quality.** Group AR₹43.4239 fell from₹57.5240, but unbilled₹58 rose from₹18.1763 and inventory₹69.1812 from₹51.8392. AP₹37.5217 versus₹29.2270 only partly funds this. All₹43.4239 disclosed receivables are in6 month-plus buckets:₹29.3189 at6–12 months,₹9.9723 at1–2 years,₹2.2059 at2–3 years and₹1.9268 over3 years, with nil allowance. The ageing basis and collection evidence deserve direct verification; nil accounting provision is not proof of zero credit loss. Inventory consists₹48.4269 traded goods and₹20.7543 WIP, also with nil diminution provision. Obsolescence, acceptance delays and unbilled recoverability can impair both earnings and borrowing base. [S01, printed162–164/174, Notes15–19/38; E03–E04.]\\n\\n**Capital bridge.** Detailed groupONWC includes AR+unbilled+inventory+supplier advances/prepaids/government operating balances+commission receivable−AP−operating current liabilities; income-tax assets and accrued deposit interest are excluded. OperatingIC adds PPE/intangibles/CWIP, operating security and margin deposits. FinancingIC equals equity including warrant cash+NCI+debt−reported cash−nonoperating loan−investment. The difference is reconciled to tax assets, accrued interest, tax/gratuity provisions and deferred tax, with small source-rounding residual separately exposed. Historical parent broad proxies cannot provide this same reliable classification; their residuals are not hidden. ΔIC is cross-checked against capex−DA+ΔONWC+other operating investment. FY26 ₹18.096CWIP commissioning is a transfer, not new cash investment. Project and acquired-capital returns remain NS; a negative or distorted denominator is never celebrated as exceptional ROIC. [S01, printed148/160–165, Notes9–19; historical_metrics.json detailed calculations; E07/E08/E13.]\\n\\n**Funding.** Gross debt₹68.8823 includes overdrafts₹23.5518, invoice factoring₹32.2300, current term maturities₹9.4342, long-term debt₹3.6169 and related loan₹0.0494. Factoring is financing, not automatically collected customer cash. Reported groupcash₹27.4615 includes deposits₹27.1717; only₹0.2898 current accounts/cash is the conservative usable floor. Separate margin deposits₹2.4385 sit in other assets and are never added again. Collateral is linked to deposits; exact freedom by account isND, so all deposits are excluded in the main model. CRISIL23 September BBB-/Stable/A3, on a standalone approach, calls liquidity adequate, but discloses91.02% average bank-line use and367.2gross-current-asset days. Of₹125rated facilities,₹23.25is cash credit,₹58.20LC/BG,₹43.55 proposed funded facilities. Proposed lines and guarantees are not cash available to finance a shortfall. Its₹9.4 annual debt-obligation estimate and positive credit view are important contrary evidence. A computed₹2.08785unused-capacity proxy is expressly uncommitted and not anApril draw permission. [S01, Notes5/8/14/17/36; S17,23September rating rationale, liquidity/facility annexure; E12–E13.]\\n\\n**Opening booked obligations.** Model operating working capital excludes tax and long provisions, so they are not silently dropped: ₹6.4064opening tax is split into₹3.1594arrears paid in bridgepre7 and₹3.2470remaining booked tax paid atY1M03. Opening gratuity₹0.4941 is paid atY1M12. These are explicit timing assumptions, with sensitivities; no current tax-asset cash credit is taken. They are separate cash uses from expenses/tax on new earnings, tracked through period/annual columns and the remaining-obligation rollforward. The₹1.6190opening deferred-tax liability is not ordinary debt or asserted presently due: default separately reserves that amount in terminal cash; month12/24/60payment sensitivities replace, not duplicate, that reserve. Possible overlap with normalized future cash taxes makes this a conservative stress, not a precise tax valuation. [S01, printed159–160 Notes7/11 and printed169 Note33; model_inputs.json/model_engine.py; E32.]\\n\\n**Share/cash claims.** March issued22,937,688;24 August promoter conversion1,030,926 makes23,968,614;13 October issue1,950,000 at₹40.03 makes25,918,614 and₹7.80585gross proceeds. Older remaining2,061,856 warrants originally₹48.50 have₹36.375balance; new2,500,000 at₹40.03 have25%upfront₹2.501875 crore and75%future₹7.505625 crore. Warrants-only potential30,480,470 is not the historical EPS denominator. The101,338share movement is resolved: FY26 directors report confirms employee-option exercise at₹10 on10February2026, already included in March shares. FY25 wording mixes563,200plan capacity and506,668underlying shares; full remaining-grant/forfeiture details are unavailable. The2024plan vests1–5years and permits exercise within3years thereafter, with grant-specific strike not below₹10. Conservatively reserving the461,862remaining plan capacity produces30,942,332economic claims with all warrants, versus30,885,800using405,330remaining grant-derived shares. Neither is asserted actual issued/outstanding. The model gives no option-proceeds credit, separates issued shares from terminal economic claims, and sensitizes0/405,330/461,862. March warrant balance₹0.7732 versus cash-flow receipt₹3.75 remains unreconciled. [S01, printed82; S02, printed83; S27, PDF10–13; E30.] Dividend₹1, paid12 October to23 September holders, is a pre-entry company cash outflow, not income for a19 October buyer. Subsequent21 October conversion is excluded by cutoff. [S01, share-capital/warrant notes andCF; S21,24August allotment; S06,13October allotment; S22, terms; S07, dividend payment; E15/E28.]\\n\\n\"","\"Valuation & Market Expectations\"","\"\\nIssued market cap is₹194.78crore. Headline groupP/E is11.99× on P&L PAT, or11.51× on the conflicting EPS/reserve PAT. EBIT less finance at25%tax gives diagnosticP/E14.30×; it does not certify owner earnings. EV uses gross debt less only usable cash, excluding the deposits, and is9.97× recurring EBITDA. This simplified EV diagnostic does not assign a market value to minority claims or net the₹1.0710nonoperating loan/₹0.0080investment, whose realization is unverified; negative book NCI−₹0.6130 is not treated as cash or an automatic reduction in claim value. It therefore is not a fully reconciled acquisition EV. Full dilution without adding future proceeds is disclosed as a claim-count diagnostic, not an EV bridge. There is no supportable unconditional entry-price range whileG2 is unresolved. [S09,19October close; S06/S21 share bridge; S01 earnings/debt/cash; historical_metrics.json valuation calculations.]\\n\\n| Assumption | Bear | Base | Bull |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\\n| Annual revenue growth |−5%|10%|18%|\\n| Operating EBIT margin |7.5%|12%|15%|\\n| Billed / unbilled days |120 /150|80 /105|65 /75|\\n| Inventory / payable days |190 /75|165 /90|135 /100|\\n| Demand-facility rollover |75%|100%|100%|\\n| Terminal nominal INR k / g |18% /0%|16% /3%|14% /4%|\\n\\n|Scenario / funding / claims|Status|First breach|Gross CAGR|Rescue shares|Rescue cash|\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n|bear/no_new_finance|ABSORBING_FIRST_BREACH|preentry/pre1|NS|0|0.00|\\n|bear/bounded_optional|ABSORBING_FIRST_BREACH|investment/Y1M02|NS|2286377|10.00|\\n|bear/bounded_optional/warrant_exercise|ABSORBING_FIRST_BREACH|investment/Y1M02|NS|2286377|10.00|\\n|base/no_new_finance|ABSORBING_FIRST_BREACH|preentry/pre1|NS|0|0.00|\\n|base/bounded_optional|ABSORBING_FIRST_BREACH|investment/Y1M06|NS|2286377|10.00|\\n|base/bounded_optional/warrant_exercise|ABSORBING_FIRST_BREACH|investment/Y1M06|NS|2286377|10.00|\\n|bull/no_new_finance|ABSORBING_FIRST_BREACH|preentry/pre1|NS|0|0.00|\\n|bull/bounded_optional|CONDITIONAL|None|13.65%|1174545|5.14|\\n|bull/bounded_optional/warrant_exercise|CONDITIONAL|None|11.04%|1174545|5.14|\\n\\nBoth base branches fail atY1M06, before even the first assumed old-warrant exercise can arrive. The explicitly paid opening tax liability brings the cash failure forward; later funding cannot cure it. Neither has an ordinary return. Bull gross CAGR is13.65% if warrants expire, but only11.04% with their exercise and dilution, below the15%hurdle before trading costs. The current quote is above both original strikes, so the no-exercise bull must not be selected as the expected outcome. The15%base-growth hurdle requires about24.33038%operating EBIT margin with warrant exercise, versus the reported recurring margin about12.17%.\\n\\nThese are **conditional funding diagnostics, not probability-weighted forecasts**. The no-new-finance branch fails in thepre-entry bridge under its conservative cash floor and supplier-before-collection order; this does not mean ROX actually defaulted inApril. It means a March balance sheet with₹0.2898free cash cannot establish an unassisted October starting state. Bounded rescue uses up to₹2.08785 new debt,₹10 crore net equity and3 million rescue shares, also constrained by40 million authorized shares after reserving known/warrant claims and461,862potential ESOP plan shares. Rescue issue price is40%below the reference quote with3%issue fee. Whole-share issuance rounds up the required amount, never creates fractional claims or an unlimited plug. All financing is counterfactual and uncommitted. New bank debt cannot redraw its ownyear5 bullet; lifetime draw capacity and facility closure are enforced.\\n\\nThe model starts31 March and traverses202 days to19 October, splitting periods at24 August conversion,12 October dividend and13 October allotment. It then simulates60 monthly investment periods plus12 monthly continuing-operation periods. Every month splits supplier/payroll outflow before collections into32cycles, with1/4/16/64/128cycle tests. Every event retains cash before/after, debt, shares and phase. Borrowing and principal financing are charged full-period ending-exposure interest; tax is conservatively based on pre-draw interest and therefore is not optimistically reduced for a new rescue. Minimum cash₹0.10 is tested on every event. First breach absorbs: no later rescue, recovery price or ordinary CAGR is assigned to a failed path.\\n\\nPending warrants cannot survive to a fictitiousyear5exercise. Default expiry paths assume no holder exercise and no future cash/dilution; because the market quote exceeds strikes, that is not a prudent expectation by itself. Separate headline exercise paths assume all old/new warrants voluntarily convert at legal monthly boundaries before their18 month expiries, issuing shares and receiving only the unpaid75%then. A future subscription cannot fix an earlier breach. The comparison prevents an apparently attractive no-exercise outcome from hiding likely dilution. The separate ESOP upper-plan claim overlay is included in terminal shares without pretending an exercise date or crediting any proceeds; it cannot fund a cash shortfall. All returns are before personal tax and gross of spread/brokerage/impact except named1/2.5/5%-each-side cost cases. Whole-lot capacity is independently restrictive.\\n\\n**Earned terminal.** ContinuingFCFF isNOPAT minus the larger of actual capex−DA+ΔONWC+additional operating deposits and the investment needed for terminalgrowth at15%incremental return. EV=FCFF/(k−g), withk>g and positiveFCFF required. A full operating year must survive without additional optional financing. The model reserves enoughyear5 cash for its worst intraperiod draw plus any unfunded incremental reinvestment requirement; the remaining opening-obligation reserve is also retained, and only excesscash is added. Debt is subtracted once, deposits remain excluded, and assumed99%owner attribution is stressed95/100% because NCI attribution is not reliably reconciled. No interim dividends are assumed, so100%of investor proceeds are terminal; this concentration is a major model risk, not a claimed present-value DCF target. Higherk/lowerg and lower-margin tests are the multiple-normalization equivalent.\\n\\n|Hurdle|Funding|Exercise|EBIT margin bracket|\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n|0.00%|no_new_finance|0|NO_FEASIBLE_SIGN_CHANGE|\\n|0.00%|no_new_finance|1|NO_FEASIBLE_SIGN_CHANGE|\\n|0.00%|bounded_optional|0|NO_FEASIBLE_SIGN_CHANGE|\\n|0.00%|bounded_optional|1|16.580831–16.580831%|\\n|12.00%|no_new_finance|0|NO_FEASIBLE_SIGN_CHANGE|\\n|12.00%|no_new_finance|1|NO_FEASIBLE_SIGN_CHANGE|\\n|12.00%|bounded_optional|0|20.818958–20.818958%|\\n|12.00%|bounded_optional|1|22.215544–22.215544%|\\n|15.00%|no_new_finance|0|NO_FEASIBLE_SIGN_CHANGE|\\n|15.00%|no_new_finance|1|NO_FEASIBLE_SIGN_CHANGE|\\n|15.00%|bounded_optional|0|22.399567–22.399567%|\\n|15.00%|bounded_optional|1|24.330381–24.330381%|\\n|18.00%|no_new_finance|0|NO_FEASIBLE_SIGN_CHANGE|\\n|18.00%|no_new_finance|1|NO_FEASIBLE_SIGN_CHANGE|\\n|18.00%|bounded_optional|0|24.443645–24.443645%|\\n|18.00%|bounded_optional|1|26.738716–26.738716%|\\n\\nEvery scan and bisection, successful or failed, is retained. There are449unique full cash paths and873labels after lossless deduplication, not only chosen endpoints. Root scans include0%price-implied break-even and12/15/18%hurdles, and cover4–30%EBIT margins with every other stated assumption fixed, and revenue-growth grids0–40%without an unwarranted continuity claim. A mathematical hurdle is not an achievable operating plan. Additional two-way matrices vary margin×terminalk and growth×unbilled days. One-way tests cover both cash-conversion assets, inventory/payables, rates, caps, rescue discount/fees, collateral release, rollover, maintenance, owner share, terminal reinvestment and warrant exercise. Model failures remain visible and never become zero-return observations in an average.\\n\\n**Execution.** All60 official sessions24 July–19 October were observed with positive traded value. Twenty-day mean/median turnover₹62.5264/₹38.1496 lakh;60 day₹35.23883/₹16.1884 lakh. The60 day median is the conservative capacity reference. A₹5 lakh notional rounds up tofive lots/8000 shares/₹6.012 lakh. At5%of conservative daily value, literal₹5 lakh takes6.18 theoretical days and whole-lot reference7.43; actual order constraints may be worse. Median33600 share volume permits0/1/2 whole lots per day at2/5/10%. Rolling-window lot capacity and censored exits are retained in liquidity.json, not replaced by fractional-lot execution. NSE defines ST as SME trade-for-trade, requiring delivery settlement rather than ordinary rolling-market netting. The dated security extract records a₹71.40–₹78.90daily range, approximately5%around the reference close. The historical10%→5%change row could not be retained as an exact primary response, so no asserted transition date is used. Neither that range nor a circuit print proves executable depth. The window contains52SM and8STsessions, including24 July and9–19 October. There is no verified spread/order-book snapshot or complete currentASM/GSM restriction notice. [S09,60dated bhavcopy rows and19October security master; S25, ST settlement; liquidity.json; E19/E24.]\\n\\n\"","\"Bear Case & Permanent-Loss Path\"","\"\\nThe strongest bear chain is hardware/project growth → inventory and unbilled acceptance delays → ageing without provisions → reduced lender borrowing base and less supplier credit → expensive rescue equity or missed obligations → permanently diluted or impaired owner value. A loss of a large customer/OEM relationship can simultaneously reduce margin and slow collections. Deposits pledged to lenders may protect creditors without protecting common shareholders. Selling inventory at a haircut and releasing receivables are not free upside: they can reduce equity recovery and future revenue. Impairment risk is **High**, with uncertainty too large for a precise probability or reliable bear recovery price. [Analyst linked stress based on S01 ageing/inventory/credit notes and S03 concentration risks; E03/E04/E12/E17.]\\n\\nThe single decisive variable is **cash realization of the billed and unbilled balances under verified funding terms**. The strongest evidence against a wholly negative interpretation is the unmodified audit, CRISILadequate-liquidity conclusion, actual fresh equity and operational delivery centres. These support further investigation, not an automatic dismissal. Conversely, a low headlineP/E or temporary share-price rebound does not reconcile owner cash. Model failure is a conditional financing boundary, not an allegation that the issuer is insolvent. [S01, unmodified audits and cash/asset notes; S17, liquidity conclusion; S06/S21, actual allotments; scenario_summary.json.]\\n\\n\"","\"5× / 10× Feasibility\"","\"\\nFive-year5× requires37.97%annual share-price growth and₹375.75;10×58.49%and₹751.50. At30,942,332conservative economic claims including the remaining-plan ESOP overlay, these require about₹1163 crore/₹2325 crore equity, before any additional rescue dilution. Even a20×terminalP/E requires roughly₹58/₹116 crore owner earnings, and at8%owner margin approximately₹727/₹1453 crore revenue. A12×multiple raises required profits further. Exact arithmetic is retained in reverse_results.json. Those outcomes require multiplefold real economic expansion, funded working capital, attractive reinvestment, resolved accounting and controlled dilution. Neither a small market cap nor broad cloud TAM supplies that evidence. Classification: **Speculative / unsupported**, not a price target or a probability claim. [Calculated from S09 price and S06/S21/S22 claim counts; reverse_results.json outcome hurdles. Not guidance.]\\n\\n\"","\"Monitoring Plan\"","\"\\n| KPI/event | Baseline | Improvement/milestone | Warning versus thesis break | Review/source |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Financial reconciliation | Borrowing embedded in CFO; owner PAT/EPS conflict | Signed line-by-line bridges to revised statements | Alert: incomplete response; break: substantiated material unreliability persists without remediation | Next audited/revised filing |\\n| Contract cash | Unbilled₹58, aged AR₹43.4239 | Acceptance dates and bank-reconciled subsequent collections | Alert: further growth above sales; break: material unrecoverable balances | Next results plus collection note |\\n| Actual liquidity | Usable floor₹0.2898, deposits₹27.1717 | Bank-confirmed free cash, lien schedule and committed undrawn lines | Alert: utilization remains near91%; break: actual unfunded due obligation | Next rating/financial update |\\n| Inventory |₹69.1812, WIP₹20.7543 | Ageing, turnover and cash-paid project completion | Alert: slower turns; break: material obsolete/unsupported inventory | Half-year/full-year notes |\\n| Service economics | Services/FMS₹16.3198 vs₹36.0863 | Paid recurring contracts, renewal/margin evidence | Alert: hardware-only sales growth; break: transition consumes capital without sustainable profit | Results and reconciled presentation |\\n| Capital deployment | CWIP commissioned, fresh preferential objects | Facility utilization and return on full capital including WC | Alert: timetable slips; break: persistent value destruction without credible correction | Proceeds/utilization filings |\\n| Warrants/claims | Warrants-only30,480,470; conservative ESOP-overlaid30,942,332 | Conversion cash/shares and expiry schedule reconcile | Alert: new dilutive proposal; break: unfair minority terms or unreconciled claims | Every allotment and shareholding filing |\\n| Governance/RPT | RP receivable₹7.1768; tax₹3.1594 arrears | Collections, arm's-length terms, cleared tax and reconciled subsidiary audit scope | Alert: balances grow; break: verified diversion/material concealment | Audit/RPT/tax disclosures |\\n| Tradeability | ST,1600lot,60 day median₹16.1884 lakh | Current restriction notice and executable depth | Alert: participation capacity falls; break: suspension/effectively no exit for intended size | Before any transaction |\\n\\nThese are research review triggers, not scheduled automations or universal mechanical sell rules. A missed quarter requires context; a documented integrity failure can change the gate immediately.\\n\\n\"","\"Final Classification & Conditional Action\"","\"\\n**Pending evidence: Hold — unresolved. Research priority, not eligible for favourable new-investment classification.** The complete v3matrix cannot be applied to invented midpoint scores. All three composites remain NS; the record belongs in a separate pending-evidence table, not at the bottom of a numeric ranking. It does not meet compounder criteria because the required scores, cash resilience and critical-gate clearance are absent.\\n\\nA price decline alone cannot clearG2. Reconciled accounts plus independently verified collections/funding could allow rescoring; a supported, cash-funded base case meeting15%after realistic execution costs would then be required. If an existing holding exists, the relevant issue is reliability/funding/liquidity, not purchase-price anchoring. Position weights, tax basis and executable depth were not supplied, so no individualized exit count, allocation or trade is inferred. No security transaction is authorized by this research.\\n\\n\"","\"Sources, Assumptions & Open Questions\"","\"\\nPrimary documents are linked below; material claims map to evidence IDs in evidence_ledger.json. Source dates and document hashes identify exactly what was read. Raw PDFs, OCR/extraction caches, private transfer helpers and Library identities are deliberately excluded from recovery archives. Authored numeric extracts preserve enough evidence, formulas and code to rebuild the full research offline; they are not claimed to replace independent reading of the linked originals.\\n\\n- S01: [FY2026 annual report](https://archives.nseindia.com/annual_reports/SME_AR_31858_ROXHITECH_2025_2026_A_3327582_08092026141331.pdf), 2026-09-08. Printed102–176: both full audit reports, KAMs, CARO, IFC, financial statements and notes; governance/statutory54–101; front-matter2–53. read primary locally.\\n- S02: [FY2025 annual report](https://archives.nseindia.com/annual_reports/SME_AR_28841_ROXHITECH_2024_2025_A_5416823_06092025204121.pdf), 2025-09-06. Printed104–176: audits/annexures, standalone118–145 and first consolidation154–176; fiscal2024 comparatives. read primary locally.\\n- S03: [IPO prospectus](https://www.rox.co.in/wp-content/uploads/investors/ROX%20-Prospectus_Final.pdf), 2023-11-13. Identity and risks pp1,23–27; business pp102–134; audited restated FY21–23 pp43–45 and F1–F45; capital, objects and RPT. read primary locally.\\n- S04: [May29 2025 earnings call transcript](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_03062025144422_intimationtranscript.pdf), 2025-06-03. pp7,13–16:20%growth aspiration, margins, receivables, project investment responses. read primary locally.\\n- S05: [June15 2026 earnings call transcript](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_18062026213513_intimationtranscript.pdf), 2026-06-18. pp2–13: NOC/SOC operational statement, seven digital transformation clients, financial and execution comments. read primary locally.\\n- S06: [October13 2026 allotment](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_13102026171735_Outcome_of_Board_meeting.pdf), 2026-10-13. pp1–2:1.95million new shares at40.03 and2.5million warrants; issued25,918,614 andfullydiluted30,480,470. read primary locally.\\n- S07: [Dividend completion](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_14102026170117_Press_release.pdf), 2026-10-14. p2:paymentOct12,recordSep23,Rs1/share,approx2.39crore. read primary locally.\\n- S08: [CRISIL rating assignment filing](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_05102026210601_Update.pdf), 2026-10-05. Rating letter and facility amounts. read primary locally.\\n- S10: [Independent director resignation](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_01102026193041_Reg_30_-_Independent_directro.pdf), 2026-10-01. Complete filing/annexures:resignation/noothermaterialreasons; no financial allegation established. read primary locally.\\n- S11: [FY26 investor presentation](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_08062026210312_investorpresentation.pdf), 2026-06-08. Customer concentration historicalFY25, positioning and FY24–26 financials. read primary locally.\\n- S12: [Dynacons FY26 annual report](https://www.dynacons.com/dynacons-annual-report-2025-26.pdf), FY2026 annual report; audit signed before cutoff. Consolidated financials and notes pp154–180; systemsintegration/managedservices. read primary locally.\\n- S13: [Dynacons FY26 presentation](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/DSSL_02062026122429_PRESENTATIONDSSLMARCH2026.pdf), 2026-06-02. pp9,23,35–36 revenue/margins/mix. read primary locally.\\n- S14: [Allied Digital FY26 presentation](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ADSL_26052026124043_CoveringLetterinvestorpresentation.pdf), 2026-05-26. pp30–36 financials,CFO,adjusted EBITDA andprovision caveat. read primary locally.\\n- S15: [Orient Technologies FY26 annual report](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/680b427b158e6c535e8eb95b/6a970274d84d48d87c12d85d_Orient%20India%20AR%202026-Final_compressed.pdf), FY2026; signed May27; available on issuer site by cutoff. Printed45 business performance;185–186 consolidated P&L and CF; segment and exceptional notes. read primary locally.\\n- S16: [Orient Q1FY27 presentation](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/680b427b158e6c535e8eb95b/6a7da53c0046e8df0a08bb12_Investor%20Presentation_Q1FY27_signed.pdf), 2026-08-12. Recent operating trajectory and economicmix. read primary locally.\\n- S09: [NSE dated