ation](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_31082026113259_Reg_30_Intimation.pdf), 2026-08-31. UBO changes from not applicable to Aditya Bhutra and Ankita Rathi. read primary locally.\\n- S24: [Investor-name clarification](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROX_2002_13102026155428_Reg_30.pdf), 2026-10-13. Ray Invest corrected to Raynvvest; other terms unchanged. read primary locally.\\n- S25: [NSE SME market sub-segments](https://www.nseindia.com/static/products-services/emerge-sme-market-segment), Current official market rules read at research; issuer series dated19October2026. ST trade-for-trade settlement and standard lots. read primary with web.\\n- S26: [Original FY24 full annual report and AGM notice](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ROXHITECH_31082024163244_AGMnotice.pdf), 2024-08-31. PDF41–45 full audit/CARO/IFC; PDF47 cashflow; printed101 Note18 FD25; printed104 Note27 historical Ingram proceeding. read primary locally.\\n- S27: [ROX Employee Stock Option Plan2024 EGM notice](https://www.rox.co.in/wp-content/uploads/investors/Rox%20-%20EGM%20Notice%20-%204-3-2024%20Final.pdf), 2024-02-28. PDF1–2 resolutions;10–13 plan ceiling, vesting, pricing, exercise and accounting. read primary locally.\\n- S28: [FY2023 AGM notice and directors report only](https://www.rox.co.in/wp-content/uploads/investors/Annual%20report%20202223.pdf), 2023-08-24. 18pages, notice dated24August/directors report21July; PDF7 highlights, PDF12–14 auditor discussion; actual audit/annexures not included. complete18-page file read; not a full audit report.\\n\\n**Priority unresolved questions:** reconcile remaining CFO/debt vintages; the FY24₹25FD cash-definition change is explained; explain+₹58.21consolidation/fixed-asset line; reconcile₹9.3501unbilled difference and subsidiary audit scope; bridge owner PAT/exceptional/EPS; verify individual deposit liens and current drawable facilities; show post-yearend collections and provisions; reconcile RPT service amounts and receivables; reconcile March warrantcash and remaining ESOP grants/forfeitures/strikes; quantify actual proceeds deployment, current customer/vendor concentration and post-allotment promoter encumbrance. FY24 full annual audit annexures were recovered and inspected; Original FY21/FY22/FY23 full annual audit reports were not independently retrieved or represented as inspected. The recovered18-page FY23 file is notice/directors material only, despite referring to an annexed audit. [S28, entire file.] The prospectus examiner reports reliance on prior FY21/FY22 auditor reports and presents audited restatedFY21–23 schedules; that is distinct from independently inspecting the originalFY23full audit and annexures. [S03, restatement examiner report F1–F3.] These are explicit research limits, not silently passed checks.\\n\\nCalculation conventions: closing working-capital days use revenue for billed/unbilled and product cost for inventory/payables, labelled accordingly. Revenue less product cost is a value-added proxy before labour and other delivery costs, not a verified segment gross margin. Normal tax25%, cost-of-capital13–17%, scenario capital intensity and rescue terms are analyst assumptions. Historical cash capex is gross purchase outflow, not netdisposals; capital transfers are not cashcapex. CF borrowing reclassification and financing-interest adjustment are shown separately. Group and parent are never spliced. No probabilities, unverified peer multiples, exact market share, invented quarterly CFO or unqualified fair value are supplied.\\n\\n**Update log.** Initial20 October2026cutoff assessment uses19 Octprice. Primary July15revisions, original FY24results/full annual audit, ESOP2024scheme, Augustconversion and JulyEGM terms were recovered during this research and incorporated before freeze. These improve evidence coverage but do not clearG2. The model was corrected before freeze to charge intraperiod rescue interest, close borrowing at maturity, expire warrants inside their legal horizon, date known pre-entry cash flows, reserve potential ESOP claims and separate the resolved FY24FD cash reclassification from still-unresolved group cash flows, and explicitly settle/reserve opening tax and gratuity obligations before calculating equity returns. These are methodology/implementation corrections, not subsequent issuer events or a manufactured score change.\\n\\n**All 16 v3 final checks:**\\n1. Identity/security/scope/date verified and explicit.\\n2. Material primary records read; management/analyst statements labelled; unavailable originals disclosed.\\n3. Audit/RPT/funding/dilution reviewed with proportionate gates, no fraud inference.\\n4. Units and periods separated; original/comparative vintages retained; no overlappingTTM.\\n5. Revenue growth separated from invoice mix, unbilled recognition and perimeter; organic unknown remains NS.\\n6. CFO/PAT uses summed numerator/denominator; capex does not excuse weak CFO; ratio comparability caveat retained.\\n7. Incremental-return numerator, fullcapital denominator, timing, residual and project IRR limitations visible.\\n8. Normalization, rent/leases, tax, NCI and dated dilution consistent and sensitized; unresolved owner PAT not hidden.\\n9. Every scenario links pre-entry/intraperiod cash, financing, reinvestment and terminal reserve; failure absorbs.\\n10. All13 canonical factors reused exactly; each composite's weights sum100%.\\n11. Missing evidence stays NS with coverage and mathematical bounds; no renormalization.\\n12. Raw/final scores reconcile; only explicit governance/funding/growth-quality overrides tested.\\n13. Classification follows gate-first rules; no unsupported compounder designation.\\n14. ₹5 lakh plus roundedwhole-lot position assessed; quote/turnover not promised execution.\\n15. Strongest bear, contrary evidence and cash-realization thesis-break variable explicit.\\n16. Samev3cutoff/tie rules apply; pending record visibly unranked, not batch-complete or a winner.\\n\\nCheck completion means the requirement was addressed, not that missing evidence is resolved. Both compact and full recovery packages must rebuild generated outputs after those outputs and attestations are removed under an offline declared-input guard. Independent verification is recorded separately and cannot be inherited from a copied badge.\\n\"","\"heading_start\"","\"body_start\"","\"end\"","\"original_heading\"","\"## 1. Executive Verdict\\n\"","\"## 2. Research Header, Gates and Data Confidence\\n\"","\"## 3. Scorecard and Calculation Audit\\n\"","\"## 4. Business Overview\\n\"","\"## 5. Moat / Industry Position\\n\"","\"## 6. Revenue Growth & Scale\\n\"","\"## 7. Growth Quality & Reinvestment Runway\\n\"","22206","\"## 8. Management, Governance & Execution\\n\"","22232","31905","\"## 9. Financial Forensics\\n\"","31944","41105","\"## 10. Valuation & Market Expectations\\n\"","41144","42651","\"## 11. Bear Case & Permanent-Loss Path\\n\"","42679","43593","\"## 12. 5× / 10× Feasibility\\n\"","43616","46085","\"## 13. Monitoring Plan\\n\"","46134","47110","\"## 14. Final Classification & Conditional Action\\n\"","47155","59808","\"## 15. Sources, Assumptions & Open Questions\\n\"","\"filename\"","\"format\"","\"content_sha256\"","\"historical_inputs.json\"","\"e97499dfd986a601913bbbdc3b6a316c0e778f17fb8da0eed59fb3e988bc93d1\"","\"Complete JSON content\"","\"472d6565e72ced82d9c854c96b60bbd379772b435fc0ab104f8cd29ec0b78d13\"","\"Authored analytical table or source register, not a bundled original filing. Source-access qualifications remain in the research.\"","\"content\"","\"b28318c1431c452042d7904638a804511c6c76b9604e3a1d5e411339015ebf95\"","\"38e1cda387499da084d25460853f42b745f7929d22deb4a513d47994d1163620\"","\"score_inputs.json\"","\"ec3ab9d360aa1950558b97d514f30abb000100d40cf72c4a92d6b036337bb596\"","\"498c7fe93d16ad1e1414a98c329fff86df46020b5bc8033fc89b697a607128dd\"","\"source_register.json\"","\"9aa8d4b75cb11b81703c7569390b2bd8a0389800731